desc: ReEQ - Parametric Graphic Equalizer (FMA Edition)
tags filters
version: 1.2.0-fma.20  //<--- Make sure you change VERSION below if this changes!!
author: Justin Johnson
license: MIT
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ReaPack metadata (FMA Series repository). The JSFX header above is the
// original ReEQ header; the tags below mirror the FMA Series conventions
// so reapack-index can parse this package and install its includes.
// @version 1.2.0
// @author Justin Johnson (original ReEQ); FMA Edition by Free Mix Audio
// @changelog
//   v1.2.0-fma.20 (2026-10-22)
//     - Bottom row centred as ONE group on the window width,
//       recomputed every frame: ECO/HQ, M/S, Scale, Gain, the
//       Mid/Side gains and phase toggles, LIMIT, PANEL, AGC and
//       SILK. The classic button widths are kept and only the
//       gaps are computed, so the full row is visible from the
//       moment the plugin opens - the SILK button no longer
//       starts half-hidden at the right edge.
//     - The theme selector moved from the top-right corner into
//       the bottom row, as its last pill after SILK; its list
//       opens upward, draws on top of the node panel, and while
//       it is open the panel ignores the mouse. Settings stays
//       alone in the corner.
//     - Base theme renamed "FMA Solid" (slider enum, list and
//       pill label); values, order and palettes untouched.
//       Audio bit-identical to fma.19.
//   v1.2.0-fma.19 (2026-10-22)
//     - NEW: SILK (hidden slider60, HQ ONLY) - a spectral
//       exciter stage inside the x2 oversampled path, after the
//       SVF cascade and before decimation. Four bands split by
//       subtraction (250 Hz / 3.5 kHz / 9 kHz) pass through
//       asymmetric tanh shapers with unity small-signal gain,
//       so steady tones keep ~0 dB of net EQ and only harmonics
//       are added: lows DEEP (strong 2nd harmonic), mids
//       DEFINED (almost no drive), highs EXPENSIVE (more drive
//       the higher they sit). Worst alias spur measured at
//       -100 dBFS; with SILK at 0 the stage is skipped whole
//       and HQ renders bit-identical to fma.18. In ECO the
//       button is drawn locked and does nothing, by design.
//     - The limiter is finished: the factory hard clamp at
//       0 dBFS is replaced by a soft ceiling at -1 dBFS -
//       bit-exact passthrough below the -3 dBFS knee, a tanh
//       curve above it that approaches the ceiling and can
//       never exceed it. No added latency (PDC 0 / 31
//       unchanged); works in both modes.
//     - Audit fix B1: the slope dial's fade read a misspelled
//       node variable that does not exist; it now reads the
//       selected node like everything else.
//   v1.2.0-fma.18 (2026-10-22)
//     - Stage 3: six full FMA themes - Fire Storm, Ice Storm,
//       Sand Storm, Star Rain, Sea Mist, Bronze Wall - plus the
//       FMA base theme and Classic, selected from the GUI pill.
//       Each theme re-palettes the WHOLE window on the fma.17
//       skin: tinted graphite ground and plate, buttons in the
//       theme accent, and the spectrum drawn with a deep body,
//       a luminous main-colour edge and near-white peaks.
//     - Theme state lives in the new hidden slider59
//       "GuiTheme", appended at the END of the slider list
//       (nothing renumbered). The selector list is drawn
//       inside the plugin and its clicks are guarded, so they
//       never create, delete or drag bands. Audio
//       bit-identical to fma.17.
//   v1.2.0-fma.17 (2026-10-21)
//     - FMA skin buttons now wear an intense orange fill
//       (#F26B1A) with a lighter hover and dark text - the
//       resting buttons no longer get lost against the graph
//       plate. Covered: the whole bottom row, Settings, the
//       GUI tab and the node panel's own buttons. State
//       colours unchanged: HQ keeps the house amber, "on"
//       toggles their green, DELETE its red.
//     - The node panel's corners are delicately rounded
//       (radius 10) in the FMA skin only; the original
//       translucency is untouched. Classic unchanged. Audio
//       bit-identical to fma.16.
//   v1.2.0-fma.16 (2026-10-21)
//     - FMA skin buttons redrawn with EXACTLY the original
//       capsule construction - only the colour values change.
//       The extra outline stroke that left two little circles
//       at the caps of every button is removed everywhere.
//       The Classic drawing path is untouched. Audio
//       bit-identical to fma.15.
//   v1.2.0-fma.15 (2026-10-21)
//     - NEW: the FMA house skin - graphite background, the
//       graph on a recessed dark plate, flat pills, the HQ
//       button and the selected node's ring in house amber -
//       with a corner tab ("GUI: FMA" / "GUI: Classic") that
//       switches skins instantly. The node panel keeps its
//       ORIGINAL translucent background, by express design
//       decision (a solid fill takes away what makes the
//       original design lovely).
//     - Skin state in the new hidden slider58 "GuiSkin",
//       appended at the END of the slider list (nothing
//       renumbered); a fresh instance opens in the FMA skin.
//       Geometry, band colours, the white curve and the RTA
//       are untouched. Audio bit-identical to fma.14.
//   v1.2.0-fma.14 (2026-10-21)
//     - Display-only correction: in HQ the drawn curve no
//       longer multiplies the filter response by the half-band
//       chain magnitude, so the graph stops reporting the
//       oversampling chain's terminal droop and ripple toward
//       the top octave. It now draws the filters' own
//       response, flat to the last pixel, like the original
//       and the reference plugins. The droop remains in the
//       AUDIO exactly as in fma.13; it is simply not drawn.
//       Audio bit-identical to fma.13.
//   v1.2.0-fma.13 (2026-10-21)
//     - HQ rebuilt with a different method: THIS EQ CARRIES
//       NO LINEAR PHASE. HQ is now x2 minimum-phase
//       oversampling with a self-contained half-band FIR
//       generated by Kaiser formula at init (125 taps,
//       stopband -109 dB, folded image residue -151 dB),
//       working at every sample rate. Latency drops from
//       2559 to 31 samples, and the dynamics' timing now
//       matches ECO. ECO bit-identical to fma.12.
//   v1.2.0-fma.12 (2026-10-19)
//     - Four corrections from review: the convolution kernel
//       of the time is built paced by samples so it no longer
//       stalls the audio thread (the design curve is drawn
//       while it builds); the graph's left edge extends down
//       to 10 Hz; dynamics processing is coalesced per band.
//   v1.2.0-fma.11 (2026-10-19)
//     - Reformulation: two quality modes only, {Eco, HQ} -
//       the x8 stage is removed after CPU reports (a single
//       instance could pin a real-time thread). A fresh
//       instance always starts in ECO.
//   v1.2.0-fma.10 (2026-10-18)
//     - Pruning of leftover machinery from retired stages,
//       and a fast dry-seeded start for the convolution
//       engine of the time.
//   v1.2.0-fma.9 (2026-10-18)
//     - The Linear Phase engine is rebuilt on partitioned
//       FFT convolution - the earlier direct kernel cost too
//       much CPU to be practical. (Engine retired in
//       fma.13.)
//   v1.2.0-fma.8 (2026-10-17)
//     - HQ x8 oversampling stage added. (Removed in fma.11
//       for CPU cost.)
//   v1.2.0-fma.7 (2026-10-17)
//     - The HQ half-band filter becomes self-contained: it
//       is generated by formula at init instead of shipping
//       fixed coefficients that only existed for 44.1 and
//       48 kHz - HQ now works at every sample rate (audit
//       B7/B8).
//   v1.2.0-fma.6 (2026-10-17)
//     - Linear Phase kernel enlarged to 4095 taps for a
//       steeper, cleaner response. (Engine retired in
//       fma.13.)
//   v1.2.0-fma.5 (2026-10-17)
//     - The dynamics action curve is drawn at the node
//       itself, so what the per-band dynamics is doing is
//       visible exactly where it happens.
//   v1.2.0-fma.4 (2026-10-16)
//     - Dynamics display at the node completed, plus node
//       panel fixes.
//   v1.2.0-fma.3 (2026-10-16)
//     - Per-band dynamics gains its own ON/OFF switch per
//       band, and real Attack/Release times replace the
//       fixed smoothing.
//   v1.2.0-fma.2 (2026-10-16)
//     - The per-band dynamics is connected end to end: the
//       original file already carried a dynamic-range
//       control per band that was stored in every project
//       but NEVER wired into the audio path (audit H1).
//       Each band now has working DYN, threshold and range.
//       A Linear Phase quality mode is added. (Retired in
//       fma.13.)
//   v1.2.0-fma.1 (2026-10-15)
//     - P0 audit fixes: the spectrum's "Full" mode no longer
//       sums L+R (+6 dB too hot) - it averages (B6); the
//       frequency mapping derives from the session's
//       Nyquist instead of a hard-coded 22050 Hz, so bands
//       land on their true Hz at 48 kHz and above (B11);
//       the HQ filter selection is deterministic per sample
//       rate (B7).
//     - The full engineering log (fma.1-fma.20) is kept
//       inside the file, below the slider definitions.
// @about
//   # ReEQ - Parametric Graphic Equalizer (FMA Edition)
//   Corrected and extended edition of ReEQ v1.2.0 by Justin Johnson,
//   released under the MIT license; original copyright and attribution
//   are preserved. Per-band dynamics, x2 minimum-phase HQ mode, SILK
//   (HQ only), a finished -1 dBFS soft-ceiling limiter, the FMA skin
//   and six full GUI themes.
//   FMA Series by Free Mix Audio.
// @provides reeq-fma-edition-deps/spectrum.jsfx-inc
// @provides Dependencies/svf_filter.jsfx-inc
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


