/* ============================================================================
   ReEQ - FMA Edition 1.2.0-fma.20
   Based on ReEQ v1.2.0 by Justin Johnson, released under the MIT license.
   Original copyright and attribution are preserved; the changes below were
   made by the FMA Series project. Nothing else was touched.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   MODIFICATION LOG (newest first):
   - 1.2.0-fma.20 (2026-10-22) BOTTOM ROW CENTRED + THEME PILL
     MOVED DOWN + BASE THEME RENAMED (Juan's notes after testing
     fma.19 in Windows: the SILK button "ha quedado en parte
     oculto en la apertura del plugin"). The old row was anchored
     to a nominal 660 px group while the real row spans 786 px,
     so it was never centred and SILK sat 5 px from the right
     edge at the 922 px design width. The whole bottom row -
     ECO/HQ, M/S, Scale, Gain, the Mid/Side gains and phase
     toggles, LIMIT, PANEL, AGC, SILK and now the theme pill -
     is laid out as ONE group centred on the window width,
     recomputed every frame (both retina branches): the classic
     button widths are kept and only the gaps are computed
     (uniform, capped at the classic spacing), so at the design
     width the full row is visible from the moment the plugin
     opens, with equal margins on both sides. The theme selector
     leaves the top-right corner (Settings stays there alone)
     and becomes the last pill of the bottom row, after SILK;
     its list now opens UPWARD from the pill, is drawn last so
     it stays on top of the node panel it can overlap, and
     while the list is open the node panel ignores the mouse.
     The base theme (GuiTheme = 0) is renamed "FMA Solid" in
     the slider enum, the list and the pill label - values,
     order and palettes are untouched. AUDIO IS BIT-IDENTICAL
     TO fma.19 (the whole fma.19 identity battery: ECO, HQ with
     Silk 0 and 100, limiter below the knee and over the
     ceiling); the diff is this log + the slider59 enum label
     + @gfx layout only. Default is ECO; a fresh instance opens
     in the FMA Solid theme.
   - 1.2.0-fma.19 (2026-10-22) FINAL STAGE (Juan's order): SILK
     (HQ ONLY) + THE FINISHED LIMITER + AUDIT FIX B1.
     SILK: a new hidden slider60 "Silk" (0..100, appended at the END
     of the slider list - nothing renumbered; default 0) drives a
     spectral-exciter stage that lives INSIDE the HQ x2 path, after
     the SVF cascade and before the half-band decimation, so its
     harmonics are generated where they have headroom and the
     decimation FIR cleans what falls out of band. In ECO the stage
     does not exist (it sits inside the oversampled branch) and its
     button is drawn locked. Design (Juan's words: brushstrokes,
     almost spectral - highs that sound EXPENSIVE, lows DEEP, mids
     DEFINED): the 2x stream is split into four bands by subtraction
     (one-pole crossovers at 250 Hz / 3.5 kHz / 9 kHz; the bands sum
     back to the input exactly); per band a pre-emphasis gain feeds
     an asymmetric tanh shaper (the house tanh - EEL2 has none) and
     a complementary de-emphasis restores unity small-signal gain,
     so the net EQ on steady tones is ~0 dB and only harmonics are
     added. The harmonic residue is computed from a half-band-
     filtered copy of the 2x stream (the exciter never sees the
     zero-stuff image, so it cannot intermodulate with it) and is
     mixed under the untouched dry path. Lows get the strong asymmetry (2nd harmonic = depth),
     mids almost no drive (definition), highs more drive the higher
     they sit. Measured at Amount 100 with -12 dBFS sines (see the
     stage notes): THD around 0.3-1% at 1 kHz. With Silk = 0 the
     stage is skipped whole and HQ renders BIT-IDENTICAL to fma.18;
     ECO is bit-identical at any Silk value. The SILK number button
     sits in the bottom bar right of AGC (drag to adjust; Ctrl +
     double-click resets to 0); in ECO it is dimmed, slashed and
     inert.
     LIMITER: the factory hard clamp at 0 dBFS is gone. When LIMIT
     is on, the output stage (both modes, still sample-by-sample
     with no memory and no latency - PDC 0 / 31 unchanged) is a
     soft ceiling at -1 dBFS (0.891251): bit-exact passthrough
     below the -3 dBFS knee (0.707946), and above it a tanh curve
     that approaches the ceiling asymptotically and can never
     exceed it. LIMIT off leaves the signal untouched.
     B1: the audit's surviving typo is fixed - the slope dial's
     fade indexed Band_Slope with a misspelled node variable that
     does not exist; it now reads the selected node like
     everything else.
     AUDIO: ECO bit-identical to fma.18 in every state; HQ
     bit-identical with Silk = 0 and LIMIT off (and below the
     limiter knee with LIMIT on).
   - 1.2.0-fma.18 (2026-10-22) STAGE 3 - SIX FMA THEMES (Juan's
     order, palettes approved by him as mocks). The corner tab is
     now the theme selector: a click opens a list drawn inside
     the panel (never gfx_showmenu - native menus land offset in
     this house) with FMA / FMA Fire Storm / FMA Ice Storm /
     FMA Sand Storm / FMA Star Rain / FMA Sea Mist /
     FMA Bronze Wall / Classic. The current entry is highlighted
     with its accent; a click on an entry applies it at once and
     closes the list; a click anywhere else just closes it; and
     list clicks are guarded so they never create bands, delete
     bands or drag nodes. The tab shows the current selection
     ("GUI: FMA", "GUI: Sea Mist", ...) and widens to fit it.
     Each theme is the fma.17 FMA skin - same contrast buttons,
     same rounded translucent node panel - re-paletted as one
     whole: a tinted graphite ground and plate, buttons / tab /
     panel pills in the theme accent with dark text, the amber
     slot (HQ mode button, selected node's ring, dial value
     arcs) in the accent lightened, the node panel border in the
     theme's main colour, and the spectrum drawn with a DEEP
     body, a luminous main-colour edge and near-white peaks
     (spectrum.jsfx-inc learned to read palette globals; with
     them off it behaves exactly as before). Theme state is the
     new hidden slider59 "GuiTheme" appended at the END of the
     slider list (nothing renumbered); slider58 "GuiSkin" still
     rules Classic, which ignores the theme entirely. The FMA
     base theme and Classic draw identically to fma.17; DELETE
     keeps its red, "on" toggles their green, and band colours
     are untouched. AUDIO IS BIT-IDENTICAL TO fma.17 (whole-PCM
     renders, ECO and HQ: flat / bell / Low Cut / High Cut /
     combo / active dynamics); the diff is this log + slider59
     + @gfx + the spectrum include's themed path. Default is
     ECO; a fresh instance opens in the FMA base theme.
   - 1.2.0-fma.17 (2026-10-21) FMA SKIN: INTENSE ORANGE BUTTONS +
     ROUNDED PANEL CORNERS (Juan's orders after testing fma.16 in
     Windows: the resting buttons "no hace mucho contraste con el
     gris de fondo" - their dark fill (0.08, 0.09, 0.11) was the
     graph plate's own colour - and the node panel's corners
     should be "ligeramente redondeadas" in his theme). In the FMA
     skin every neutral button now wears an intense orange fill
     (0.95, 0.42, 0.10) #F26B1A - Juan asked for MORE intense than
     the approved mock's burnt orange - with a lighter orange
     hover (1.00, 0.52, 0.18) and dark text (0.10, 0.075, 0.05).
     Covered: the whole bottom row (mode in ECO, M/S, scale, the
     gain and phase buttons, LIMIT and AGC while off), Settings,
     the "GUI:" tab AND the node panel's own buttons (the
     BYPASS / shape / slope / channel column, the "< N >"
     selector and LISTEN - Juan's express reminder; they share the
     same drawing functions). States that do NOT change: the mode
     button in HQ keeps the house amber with its dark text; "on"
     toggles keep the Alpha green with bone text (e.g. PANEL);
     DELETE keeps its red; dial arcs, the selected node's ring,
     band colours, the RTA and the white curve are untouched, and
     so are the graphite ground and the graph plate. The node
     panel's corners are delicately rounded (radius 10) in the
     FMA skin only: the translucent fill is painted scanline by
     scanline as a filled rounded rectangle with the same colour
     and alpha (gfx_roundrect never fills), and the border
     follows the same radius; no inner element moves and the
     translucency is untouched. The Classic skin is byte-identical
     in execution (original colours, square panel). AUDIO IS
     BIT-IDENTICAL TO fma.16 (whole-PCM renders, ECO and HQ:
     flat / bell / Low Cut / High Cut / combo / active dynamics);
     the diff is @gfx + this log. Default is ECO; a fresh
     instance opens in the FMA skin.
   - 1.2.0-fma.16 (2026-10-21) FMA SKIN BUTTONS REDRAWN (Juan's note
     after testing fma.15: "los botones de mi tema quiero que sean
     iguales al original, solo deben mantener el color que le has
     puesto; veo que tiene como dos esferitas a las orillas de cada
     boton, eso le resta vista"). In the FMA skin every button - the
     bottom row, Settings, the "GUI:" tab and the node panel's inner
     pills - is now drawn with EXACTLY the original capsule
     construction (one filled capsule, its caps fused with the
     body), changing only the colour values to the approved FMA
     palette: the extra outline stroke that fma.15 added in the FMA
     skin (two unfilled circles at the caps - the "little spheres"
     at the edges) is removed everywhere, and the fma_pill_outline
     helper is gone. The fill, hover, bone text, amber HQ state and
     Alpha-green "on" colours are unchanged. The Classic skin's
     drawing path is byte-identical to fma.15, and the node panel
     keeps its original translucent background. AUDIO IS
     BIT-IDENTICAL TO fma.15 (whole-PCM renders, ECO and HQ: flat /
     bell / Low Cut / High Cut / combo / active dynamics); the diff
     is @gfx + this log. Default is ECO; a fresh instance opens in
     the FMA skin.
   - 1.2.0-fma.15 (2026-10-21) NEW GUI SKIN + SKIN TAB (Juan's order,
     after approving the mockups). An optional skin with the tendency
     of the FMA Series, drawn entirely in @gfx: graphite background
     (0.13, 0.14, 0.16); the graph sits on a recessed dark plate
     (0.08, 0.09, 0.11) with a fine (0.30, 0.32, 0.36) border; flat
     pills (recessed dark fill + border, bone text; the "on" state is
     the Alpha green PANEL already used); the ECO/HQ button wears the
     house amber (0.92, 0.72, 0.35) with dark text while in HQ; the
     selected node's ring is amber. The node panel keeps its ORIGINAL
     translucent background (Juan's express order: a solid fill
     "le quita lo lindo del diseno original") and only takes the
     accents: amber dial value arcs, darkened translucent pills, bone
     texts; DELETE keeps its red. The RTA, the band colours/fills, the
     white total curve, the fonts and ALL geometry and click areas are
     unchanged. A small tab in the top-right corner (left of Settings,
     labelled "GUI: FMA" / "GUI: Classic") switches the skin
     instantly; that corner is architected as the future RTA-theme
     corner of Stage 3 (today it only switches the skin - no RTA
     themes yet). The "Classic" skin is the exact v32 drawing (same
     code path, same colours). The skin state persists in a new hidden
     slider58 "GuiSkin" appended at the END of the slider list
     (nothing renumbered); a fresh instance opens in the FMA skin.
     AUDIO IS BIT-IDENTICAL TO fma.14 (whole-PCM renders, ECO and HQ:
     flat / bell / Low Cut / High Cut / combo / active dynamics); the
     diff is @gfx + the appended slider + this log. Default is ECO.
   - 1.2.0-fma.14 (2026-10-21) DISPLAY-ONLY CORRECTION (Juan's order after
     testing fma.13 against Bertom EQ Curve Analyzer: ECO matched the
     analyzer exactly, but in HQ the drawn curve showed a ripple toward
     the top octave and a terminal fall at the right edge that Bertom
     does not show - "que el grafico no lo reporte hacia el final de
     los agudos"). The total-curve drawing no longer multiplies the
     filter response by the half-band chain magnitude (fma_hb_mag):
     like the original ReEQ and the Tukan fork, the graph now draws the
     response of the filters themselves, flat to the last pixel at the
     right edge. The droop still exists in the AUDIO exactly as in
     fma.13 (-0.1 dB at 22.24 kHz, -1 dB at 23 kHz, -6 dB at 24 kHz at
     48 kHz - the half-band transition); it is simply not drawn, as in
     the reference plugins. The terminal ripple went with the same
     factor: with a flat EQ the SVF product is exactly 1.0 in both
     modes, so every non-flatness of the fma.13 HQ drawing entered
     through that single multiplication (its table, checked by numeric
     replica, is flat to 21 kHz and then dives in coarse log pixels).
     AUDIO IS NOT TOUCHED: renders bit-identical to fma.13 (whole
     files, decoded PCM) in ECO and HQ - flat, bell +6 at 1 kHz, Low
     Cut, High Cut, LC+HC combo and active dynamics. PDC unchanged:
     ECO 0 / HQ 31. fma_hb_mag and its display table remain in the
     file, unused by any drawing path (no pruning in this pass).
   - 1.2.0-fma.13 (2026-10-21) HQ REBUILT WITH A DIFFERENT METHOD (Juan's
     order after testing fma.12: RT CPU 82.9% with a 1109 ms longest RT
     block on his machine - "reprograma con otro metodo el HQ, no quiero
     que sea Linear Phase", pointing at Tukan's EQ 1.1). The ENTIRE
     linear-phase engine of fma.9-fma.12 is REMOVED: 4095-tap kernel,
     partitioned-FFT convolution, sample-paced kernel builds, measured-
     response display table, delta seed, dynamics-triggered rebuilds,
     PDC 2559. HQ is now x2 MINIMUM-PHASE OVERSAMPLING - the method of
     the original ReEQ / Tukan fork: zero-stuffing, the existing SVF
     cascade runs at 2x (SAMPLE_RATE = 2*srate), then decimation
     through a half-band FIR. Deliberate differences from Tukan/original:
     (1) the half-band is GENERATED BY FORMULA at @init (Kaiser window,
     design attenuation 108 dB, beta 10.9417; self-contained - no
     firhalfband import, no per-rate tables); (2) 125 taps instead of
     65 - with the pair decimation scheme the centre tap must sit on an
     even index or the flat identity is not exact and the delay is not
     an integer: PDC is 31 samples, measured by impulse (ECO stays 0);
     (3) the x2 stays ACTIVE AT EVERY SAMPLE RATE (no >= 88.2 kHz
     shutoff). Dynamics in HQ now run per-sample inside the 2x cascade,
     exactly like ECO - there is no kernel to rebuild: measured latency
     after a level step is 0.095 s in HQ, identical to ECO (fma.12 HQ
     took 0.32-0.36 s). The HQ display draws the real chain response:
     SVF magnitudes with the 2x coefficients multiplied by the
     generated half-band's own response (table computed from the
     generated taps), so the edge droop is drawn as it sounds. ECO->HQ
     switching is now only a PDC change (0 <-> 31): no build, no
     silence, no wait. Measured in the lab at 48 kHz: ECO bit-identical
     to fma.12 (5/5 configs, whole renders). Against the ORIGINAL ReEQ
     with identical settings, the HQ curves agree to <= 0.003 dB in the
     passband once the known FMA frequency-mapping difference is
     compensated (B11: real Nyquist vs the original's fixed 22050 - the
     same slider % gives 1000.5 Hz here, 951.6 Hz there; the raw delta,
     0.30 dB at the bell skirt, exists identically in ECO). At the edge
     this build attenuates LESS than the original (HC at the same real
     frequency: +0.26 dB at 22 kHz, +0.72 dB at 23 kHz relative) - the
     longer half-band's narrower transition. Image rejection: stopband
     of the generated half-band -109 dB (27-69 kHz); I/Q separation at
     11.52 kHz (image at 36.48 kHz) measures the folded residue at
     -151 dB rel. Live CPU (Dummy Audio, lab VM, per-block DSP span):
     HQ flat 675 us, HQ with LC+HC 821 us, during drags 823 us, with
     dynamics active 816 us, 16 bands 3025 us per 512-sample block
     (budget 10667 us); at 1024: comb 1714 us, 16 bands 4697 us.
     REAPER's own meter with five instances loaded (three HQ-class):
     RT CPU 11.3%, 0 xruns, per-FX 15% (dynamic bell) / 32% (16 bands)
     vs 12% for fma.12's LP with the same comb. fma.12's steady cost
     was similar - what is gone is its build transients: there is
     nothing left to rebuild. Default remains ECO.
   - 1.2.0-fma.12 (2026-10-19) FOUR CORRECTIONS (Juan's fma.11 video review).
     (1) SAMPLE-PACED BUILD, ~6x faster: the HQ kernel builder used to run
     fixed budgets per @block - 53 @blocks total (audio settled at 49,
     display at 53), i.e. 1.05/1.13 s at a 1024 buffer, and continuous
     drags chained rebuilds so the curve jumped in steps. Now every phase
     advances by PROCESSED SAMPLES (rate x samplesblock, with fractional
     carry), so a full build always takes ~9600 samples (~0.2 s at 48 kHz)
     at ANY buffer size. Measured with an instrumented build (blips at the
     bank flip and at display completion): ECO->HQ switch settles audio
     AND display in 0.119 s at buffer 512 and 0.108 s at buffer 1024 (the
     two buffers differ by 9%, proving sample pacing); a mid-stream rebuild
     (drag end / add / delete node) settles in ~0.10 s. Atomic bank flip
     and phase order are unchanged. (2) DISPLAY DURING BUILD = DESIGN
     CURVE: while a build is in flight, the HQ display draws the analytic
     design curve (the same path ECO uses), so the graph follows the
     controls instead of freezing on a stale table and jumping in steps;
     when the build completes, the kernel's measured table takes over.
     Coordination uses a stable generation counter written only at phase
     completion (fma_lp_disp_gen vs fma_lp_dirty_gen) - no hot mutable
     variables shared between @gfx and @sample, no double drawing, RTA
     untouched. (3) LEFT EDGE: the measured-response grid reference moves
     20 -> 10 Hz (phase-3 measurement, its three initializations, the
     srate-change branch, and the display interpolation/clamp), so with a
     Low Cut the white total curve follows the cut down to the 10 Hz graph
     edge with no flat segment (was: a flat octave 10-20 Hz, 8.5 dB display
     error at 10 Hz with a cut at 18.9 Hz; audio was always correct).
     (4) COALESCED DYNAMICS: a detector change arriving with a build in
     flight lets that build finish, then chains exactly ONE fresh build
     with the latest DynApplied - no races, no stale intermediate rebuilds.
     The trigger threshold is unchanged (0.004 dB). Measured with a level
     step on a dynamic band (Peak 1 kHz, -12 dB range, 10 ms attack):
     HQ dynamics now settle 0.36 s @512 / 0.32 s @1024 after the step
     (was 1.02 s = 96 @blocks in fma.11 with the same test; ECO = 0.09 s).
     Untouched: ECO is bit-identical to fma.11; HQ steady-state audio is
     bit-identical to fma.11 (flat / Low Cut / High Cut / bell / combo);
     PDC 0 (ECO) / 2559 (HQ); delta-seeded dry start (dry audio from
     sample 0 when entering HQ); serialization; MIT attribution; the rest
     of the GUI.
   - 1.2.0-fma.11 (2026-10-19) REFORMULATION (Juan: "elimina todo lo de HQ
     actual y lo que corresponde a LP solo renombralo a HQ; asi lo dejamos
     original, ECO y HQ"). Two Quality modes again, like the original ReEQ:
     (1) REMOVED: the HQ x8 oversampling engine is gone entirely - the
     half-band FIR chain (1023/257/257 taps), its tap design and chain
     measurement, the oversampled audio path and its display table. HQ no
     longer costs more than the rest: there is no oversampling anymore.
     (2) RENAMED: HQ is now the former Linear Phase engine - 4095-tap kernel
     by partitioned FFT convolution (P=512), PDC 2559 samples
     (REAPER-compensated), display drawn from the kernel's measured response,
     per-node dynamics active, delta-seeded fast start (dry audio from
     sample 0, EQ settled in ~0.84 s at 48 kHz). The bottom-bar button
     cycles ECO <-> HQ only; all "Linear Phase" labels now read "HQ".
     (3) SESSION MIGRATION: saved Quality values map as 0 -> ECO, 1 -> HQ,
     2 -> HQ (any value >= 1 becomes HQ). Old sessions load without errors.
     Note: sessions saved with the old HQ (x8) now play through the HQ
     linear-phase engine instead - the sound changes by design, as ordered.
     ECO audio is bit-identical to fma.10; the new HQ is bit-identical to
     fma.10's Linear Phase in steady state (verified by render).
   - 1.2.0-fma.10 (2026-10-18) Pruning + fast dry start (Juan: "si hay un punto
     en el que debas borrar algo para mejorarlo, adelante, pero debe
     finalizarse"). Two things change for the user; everything else sounds
     identical to fma.9:
     (1) PRUNING: dead code removed from the LP builder — the unused 4x4095
     time-domain kernel mirror (the display now reads the shadow kernel
     directly), 16 dead Mid/Side-only branches, and unused helpers. The final
     kernel is bit-identical (same values, same summation order); ECO/HQ are
     bit-identical; LP steady state is bit-identical.
     (2) FAST DRY START: entering Linear Phase no longer plays ~2.4 s of
     silence while the kernel builds. The partition banks are seeded with a
     delta spectrum on LP entry, so you hear the dry signal immediately
     (bit-identical to the input), and the EQ fades in when the kernel is
     ready (~0.8 s at 48 kHz). The build itself is also faster (higher
     per-block budgets: no stalls, same kernel).
   - 1.2.0-fma.9 (2026-10-18) Stage 2.7 - Juan's Linear Phase CPU report
     ("tarda demasiado tiempo en procesar", fan at full speed): the LP engine
     is rewritten from direct convolution to partitioned FFT convolution.
     Convolving the 4095-tap kernel directly (2048 MACs/channel/sample) cost
     44x ECO; 60 s of audio rendered in 330 s on the lab VM. The new engine
     uses uniform partitions (P=512, FFT-1024, per-channel frequency delay
     lines, overlap-add reconstruction) and is bit-identical to the direct
     engine in steady state: LP flat, Low Cut 12.3 Hz, High Cut 19.6 kHz,
     bell +6 dB @1 kHz all render max|diff| = 0.0000000 vs fma.8, and a
     65-point dense grid over a complex curve agrees to 0.0000 dB everywhere.
     Same 4095-tap kernel and construction, same quasi-static dynamics (the
     2.3 suite converges to -21.7 dBFS without clicks), shadow-bank partition
     rebuild with no clicks. PDC 2047 -> 2559 samples (kernel 2047 + one
     512-sample block; REAPER-compensated, verified by impulse: symmetric
     response, peak at the aligned position). CPU: the 60 s LP project now
     renders in 13 s (was 330 s). ECO and HQ audio are bit-identical to
     fma.8. Known: entering LP (or starting a render) takes ~2 s before audio
     appears while the kernel builds (v26 took ~1 s; the rebuild logic is
     unchanged from v26).
   - 1.2.0-fma.8 (2026-10-17) Stage 2.6 - Juan: "haz oversampling y retira esa
     pendiente" (the -3.97 dB dive at 0.99*Nyquist in HQ flat, fma.7). HQ now
     runs at 8x: three cascaded half-band stages (1x<->2x 1023-tap Kaiser
     beta=8.0, 2x<->4x and 4x<->8x 257-tap Kaiser beta=8.0), all designed by
     formula in @init, polyphase in both directions. A longer FIR on stage 1
     is what removes the droop (the composite baseband response near the
     session Nyquist is dominated by the 1x<->2x stage); N=257 for stages 2/3
     keeps the total group delay an exact integer. HQ flat now matches ECO
     +/-0.002 dB all the way to 0.99*Nyquist (was -3.97 dB); the SVF runs at
     8x so it tracks the analog prototype even closer. HQ display redrawn
     from the REAL 8x chain response measured through the exact sample path.
     PDC 127 -> 607 samples (REAPER-compensated, measured by impulse).
     Image rejection ~-105 dB. ECO and Linear Phase audio bit-identical to
     fma.7. HQ CPU is several times higher (8x SVF + longer FIRs); per Juan,
     HQ is the mastering mode and ECO the mixing mode.
   - 1.2.0-fma.7 (2026-10-17) Stage 2.5 - Juan's "horriblemente mal en agudos"
     report (2026-10-17, testing fma.6 on his Windows vs Cockos ReaEQ: High Cut
     12 dB @19.6 kHz in ECO/HQ/Linear). Lab diagnosis (dense 65-sine grid,
     20 Hz-0.99*Nyquist, 48/44.1 kHz): Linear audio was CORRECT (LP vs ECO
     <=0.003 dB @48k, <=0.012 dB @44.1k - the "strange" LP was the display
     clipping its measured curve at 20 kHz); the REAL defect was HQ: the
     original chain (zero-insert without interpolation + one pass of a
     65-tap halfband FIR) leaked the first image back into the baseband
     (+32 dB at 23.76 kHz: audio -18.9 dB where ECO/LP give -51.0) and the
     HQ display hid it (drew -55.4 dB, 36 dB off).
     * NEW HQ oversampling: 255-tap half-band FIR, Kaiser beta=8.0, designed
       by formula in @init (I0 via series, exact unity-DC normalization),
       polyphase in BOTH directions - real interpolation on the way up,
       filtered decimation on the way down (was zero-insert + one crude
       pass). Image rejection ~-100 dB; HQ now flat like ECO to the Nyquist
       edge. PDC 16 -> 127 samples (REAPER-compensated, measured by impulse).
       Rate-normalized: correct at any rate where oversampling applies
       (<88.2 kHz).
     * FIXED HQ display vs audio: draws the REAL composite chain response
       (measured from the generated taps through the exact sample path),
       display vs audio <=0.1 dB to 0.99*Nyquist.
     * FIXED LP display edge: the measured-kernel curve now extends to
       0.99*Nyquist (was clipped at 20 kHz). LP audio untouched.
     * (no changes to ECO DSP; no changes to LP audio; no changes to
       serialization; sessions from fma.1..fma.6 load as-is)
   - 1.2.0-fma.6 (2026-10-17) Stage 2.4 - Juan's "cortes se comportan raro"
     report (2026-10-17, testing fma.5 on his Windows with Bertom: Low Cut
     12.3 Hz/12 dB + High Cut ~16-18 kHz; LP showed a -1.2 dB bass depression
     20-150 Hz that ECO didn't, HQ treble knee earlier than ECO/LP, and the
     LP display didn't show the bass depression). Lab-measured baseline
     (stepped sines, 48/44.1 kHz): ECO/HQ/LP identical in v22 and v23 (no
     fma.5 regression); ECO audio = display (SVF) to 0.01 dB; HQ audio =
     display @2x within 0.13 dB (decimation FIR droop); LP = ECO in treble
     but the 511-tap kernel smears bass cuts (12.3 Hz cut: -1.20 dB @20 Hz
     measured vs -0.56 ideal); the ECO-vs-HQ treble difference is inherent
     (less bilinear warping at 2x, HQ is closer to the analog ideal).
     * NEW long Linear-Phase kernel: 4095 taps (was 511), PDC 2047 samples
       (~42.7 ms @48 kHz), 8193-bin magnitude grid, rectangular window (the
       Hann window was measured to destroy bass cuts: -9.6 dB at DC for a
       12.3 Hz cut vs -32.2 dB rectangular), symmetric convolution (2048
       MACs/channel), sparse IDCT (only bins where the magnitude differs
       from 1) so the build stays viable in @block. Measured: 12.3 Hz/12 dB
       cut in LP now -0.26 dB @20 Hz (was -1.20), -0.31 @30 Hz (was -1.16),
       within 0.3 dB of the SVF ideal; 30/100 Hz cuts essentially perfect.
     * FIXED LP display vs audio: the total curve in Linear Phase now draws
       the kernel's MEASURED response (computed during the build), not the
       SVF ideal, so what Juan sees is what Bertom measures.
     * FIXED HQ display vs audio: the HQ total curve now includes the
       decimation FIR droop (-0.13 dB @20 kHz), so display matches audio
       within 0.02 dB in HQ.
     * (no changes to ECO/HQ DSP; no changes to serialization; sessions
       from fma.1..fma.5 load as-is)
   - 1.2.0-fma.5 (2026-10-17) Stage 2.3 - Juan's corrections on v1.2.0-fma.4
     (reported 2026-10-17 testing fma.4 on his Windows, Peak node 5.71 kHz /
     Gain 0.00 / Q 1.74 / DYN -9.4 / THR -45, applied -3.9 dB, Linear Phase):
     * FIXED dynamics visualization locality: the live curve and the range
       fill used to add DynApplied / the DYN range as a constant dB offset at
       EVERY frequency, so with static Gain 0 the indicator drew a horizontal
       line across the whole graph. Now, per armed band, the band's gfx copy
       is temporarily reconfigured (inside @gfx only, always restored after)
       and the REAL SVF magnitude is sampled at three gains - static
       (Band_Gain*Scale/100), static + DynApplied (live curve), static + DYN
       range (fill edge). Outside the band's zone of influence the three
       curves coincide, so the fill and the live line only appear around the
       node. Same formula as the DSP gain (fma_dyn_set).
     * FIXED dynamics in Linear Phase: turning DYN ON/OFF or editing
       DYN/THR/ATK/REL marked only DynForce, never the LP kernel dirty, so in
       LP the audio (and any analyzer) ignored dynamics until a node click
       rebuilt the kernel. Now fma_block_maintain() marks fma_lp_dirty +
       fma_lp_dirty_gen whenever DynApplied changes (armed branch, >0.004 dB
       step or forced) and when it resets to 0 (disarmed branch) - every real
       dynamics trigger converges through a change of DynApplied, so no GUI
       handler needed patching. The 2.1 generation counter still guarantees
       exactly one fresh build after an in-flight one, so the kernel always
       converges to the latest DynApplied. In LP the tracking is
       quasi-static (one kernel rebuild of lag), never sample-accurate like
       ECO/HQ; dynamics are NEVER inert/disabled in LP (Pro-Q 4 parity, by
       Juan's express decision 2026-10-17). The old Etapa 2 note claiming
       "dynamics are inert (static gains)" in LP is superseded by this fix.
     * (no changes to serialization; sessions from fma.1..fma.4 load as-is)
   - 1.2.0-fma.4 (2026-10-16) Stage 2.2 - Juan's visualization + panel
     corrections on v1.2.0-fma.3 (dynamics, ATK/REL, Linear Phase all
     confirmed working by Juan; this round is visualization/geometry only,
     audio bit-identical to fma.3):
     * NEW dynamics action visualization on the graph, per dynamics-armed
       band: a translucent fill in the band's color between the band's static
       curve and its full-range curve (static shifted by the signed DYN
       range), plus a LIVE curve line = static curve shifted by the band's
       current applied dynamic gain (read read-only from DynApplied, the same
       value the DSP sums into the filter). The band's node color is reused;
       the selected band draws on top. A small live-applied-dB readout sits
       under the DYN dial in the panel.
     * Panel 108 -> 124 design px tall. The left column is now FOUR
       STANDARD-SIZED pills (BYPASS / type / channel / DYN ON), all 88px
       wide, sharing one fixed small-pill height; the cut-only slope pill
       becomes a 5th uniform pill below the type pill when relevant. DYN ON
       moved OUT from under the DYN dial into the column as the 4th button,
       so it can never touch the dial again (it used to clip the panel's
       bottom edge). The 7-dial row shifted right (+30) with 64px spacing;
       the DYN dial keeps 18px of clear air from the column.
     * (no DSP changes; no new serialized state)
   - 1.2.0-fma.3 (2026-10-16) Stage 2.1 - Juan's corrections on v1.2.0-fma.2:
     * FIXED the dead DYN knob: the 112px filter-type selector pill overlapped
       the left half of the DYN dial, so clicks there opened the type menu
       instead of dragging; plus a +-0.5 dB snap dead-zone swallowed small
       drags. The selector is now 58px wide and can never reach the DYN knob.
     * NEW per-band dynamics ON/OFF button in the band panel (under the DYN
       dial), driving the same Band_DynOn flag as the node menu's "Dynamic"
       row. OFF preserves the DYN knob value; dynamics are inert while off.
       New bands default to OFF. Sessions saved by fma.2 migrate: bands with
       non-zero range load as ON.
     * Dynamics section completed: DYN + THR + ATTACK (0.5..250 ms, def 10)
       + RELEASE (5..1000 ms, def 100) dials per band. The detector now uses
       per-band envelope coefficients (DetAtk/DetRel); the old global
       10/100 ms constants are gone.
     * Panel layout: same 640x108 panel; all dials -10% (FREQ/Q/DYN/THR/ATK/
       REL 20->18, GAIN 30->27); seven dials re-spaced so nothing collides.
     * Linear Phase responsiveness: the 65-block incremental kernel rebuild
       restarted on every parameter change, so during drags it never finished
       (perpetual lag) and entering LP took ~0.75 s. Now: a 2048-entry cosine
       table is precomputed once at load (no cos() in the build loop), the
       kernel builds into SHADOW buffers and swaps atomically at completion,
       in-flight builds are never restarted (a pending change queues one more
       build), and chunk sizes are tuned so a full rebuild completes in a
       bounded number of blocks. pdc_delay stays exactly 255; 511 taps kept.
     * FIXED during lab verification (2026-10-16): a build that finished while
       new changes were pending cleared the dirty flag unconditionally, so the
       queued fresh build never ran and the live kernel stayed stale after a
       drag. Now a build-generation counter reopens exactly one fresh build
       when changes arrive mid-build; the kernel always converges to the last
       parameter values (measured <= 395 ms after the last change).
   - 1.2.0-fma.2 (2026-10-16) Stage 2 - per-band dynamics + Linear Phase:
     * A: Band_Dynamic_Range (audit finding H1, previously assigned and
       serialized but never used) now drives real per-band dynamic gain.
       Detector: peak envelope on a bandpass tap at the band's own freq/Q
       (10 ms attack / 100 ms release defaults), threshold per band
       (Band_Dynamic_Thr, -60..0 dB, default -24, serialized in v110).
       Law: over = max(0, level - thr); dyn = over * (range/24), clamped
       to +-24 dB; range > 0 = dynamic boost, range < 0 = dynamic cut,
       range = 0 = band fully static. The offset is added to the band's
       static gain through the existing 30 ms interpolator (no zipper).
       GUI: DYN (-24..+24, default 0) and THR dials in the band panel,
       Dynamic on/off row in the node right-click menu (remembers the last
       non-zero value per band).
     * B: third Quality mode "Linear Phase" (ECO/HQ/Linear Phase). A
       symmetric 511-tap FIR is built from the TOTAL magnitude response:
       every active band's svf_magnitude is evaluated on a 2048-point
       grid, combined per bin into a 2x2 channel matrix (Stereo/Left/
       Right/Mid/Side respected), and a closed-form inverse DFT yields
       the zero-phase impulse, shifted to tap 255, Hann-windowed and
       symmetrized. The kernel rebuilds incrementally in @block whenever
       bands change; pdc_delay = 255 exactly. Direct time-domain
       convolution (no FFT: REAPER's fft builtins are no-ops outside
       @gfx in this build). In Linear Phase the Listen path keeps the
       zero-latency SVF chain; dynamics stay active: the kernel rebuilds to
       track DynApplied (quasi-static, corrected in fma.5 - the old "inert"
       note is superseded).
   - 1.2.0-fma.1 (2026-10-15) Stage 1.5 - P0 audit fixes (see reeq-audit-v1.md):
     * B7: HQ FIR coefficient selection is now explicit and deterministic
       (new load_FIR_for_rate()): the 48 kHz family keeps its own table,
       every other rate uses the canonical normalized 44100 half-band
       (correct at any rate by construction - cutoff at 1/4 of the 2x rate).
       Selection runs in @init AND set_oversample() instead of a hardcoded
       @init load plus a partial branch.
     * B6: Spectrum "Full" mode now averages (L+R)*0.5 like the other modes
       (it summed L+R, reading +6 dB higher than Mid/Side on the same
       signal). Pre-EQ, post-EQ and listen feeds fixed.
     * B11: MAX_FREQ and spectrum.max_freq now derive from srate/2 at
       runtime (were hardcoded to 22050 Hz); graph mapping, node placement,
       cursor readout and the analyzer grid are correct at 48 kHz and above.
       The rate is reconciled in @block (the only place the true rate is
       reliable - @init/@slider can observe 44100 during offline renders),
       re-deriving the slider->Hz mapping and refreshing the filters.
       spectrum.jsfx-inc ships modified in Dependencies-fma/.
     * B8: at 88.2 kHz and above the HQ option is shown grayed out
       (unselectable) with an honest label instead of silently behaving as
       ECO; Quality is clamped to ECO at those rates (also reconciled in
       @block, where the true rate is known).
   ============================================================================ */

import reeq-fma-edition-deps/spectrum.jsfx-inc
import Dependencies/svf_filter.jsfx-inc

in_pin:left input
in_pin:right input
in_pin:sc input left
in_pin:sc input right
out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

options:no_meter

@init

// This should be the same as in the comment header
#VERSION = "1.2.0-fma.20";

gfx_ext_retina  = 1;
ext_nodenorm    = 1;
ext_noinit = 1;
last_gfx_ext_retina = -1;

/*
 * Initialise memory allocator
 */
function init_memory() instance(index) ( 
  index = 0;
);

/*
 * Allocate memory
 */
function alloc_memory(amount) instance(index) local(i) ( 
  i = index;
  index += amount;
  i;
);

/*
 * Round number up or down
 */
function round(in) (
  floor(in + 0.5 * sign(in));
);

/*
 * Standard log2
 */
function log2(x) ( 
  log(x) / log(2);
);

/*
 * Return string of integer
 */
function int2str(intIn) local (outStr) (
  strcpy(outStr=#,"");
  sprintf(outStr,"%d",intIn);
  outStr;
);

/*
 * Get gain (for filters) from dB
 */
function db_to_gain(db) ( 
    10^(db / 40);
);

function RMS_init(buffer_index, buffer_size)
    instance(rms_sum, rms_buffer, rms_bufIdx, rms_prev_val, rms_max_count)
( 
    rms_sum = 0;
    rms_buffer = buffer_index;
    rms_bufIdx = 0;
    rms_prev_val = 0;
    rms_max_count = buffer_size;
    memset(rms_buffer , 0, rms_max_count);
);

function RMS_reset()
    instance(rms_sum, rms_buffer, rms_bufIdx, rms_prev_val, rms_max_count)
( 
    rms_sum = 0;
    rms_bufIdx = 0;
    rms_prev_val = 0;
    memset(rms_buffer , 0, rms_max_count);
);

function RMS_process(s0, s1)
    instance(rms_sum, rms_buffer, rms_bufIdx, rms_prev_val, rms_max_count)
    local(rms_ampL, rms_ampR, rms_amp)
( 
    rms_ampL = abs(s0);
    rms_ampR = abs(s1);

    // Epsilon clamp required
    rms_ampL < 0.0000001 ? rms_ampL = 0.0000001;
    rms_ampR < 0.0000001 ? rms_ampR = 0.0000001;

    rms_amp = (rms_ampL * rms_ampL + rms_ampR * rms_ampR) * 0.5;

    rms_sum += rms_amp;
    rms_prev_val = rms_buffer[rms_bufIdx];
    rms_buffer[rms_bufIdx] = rms_amp;

    rms_bufIdx += 1;

    rms_bufIdx == rms_max_count ? (
        rms_bufIdx = 0;
    );

    rms_sum  -= rms_prev_val;
    rms_sum < 0 ? rms_sum = 0.0;
);

function RMS_getDB()
    instance(rms_sum, rms_max_count)
    local(rms_delta, rms_db)
( 
    rms_delta = rms_sum / rms_max_count;
    rms_db = 20 * log10(sqrt(rms_delta));
    rms_db;
);

/*
 * Color object
 */
function create_color(r, g, b)
  instance(red, green, blue) (
  red = r / 255;
  green = g / 255;
  blue = b / 255;
);

/*
 * Set oversampling rate including PDC
 */
/*
 * FMA fma.19: house tanh (EEL2 has no tanh()). Used by the Silk
 * shapers and the soft-ceiling limiter.
 */
function fma_tanh(fma_th_x) local(fma_th_e) (
  fma_th_x > 10 ? 1 : fma_th_x < -10 ? -1 : (
    fma_th_e = exp(2 * fma_th_x);
    (fma_th_e - 1) / (fma_th_e + 1);
  );
);

/*
 * FMA fma.19: Silk stage coefficients, recomputed whenever
 * set_oversample() (re)sets SAMPLE_RATE - the stage runs at 2x, so
 * the one-pole corners are derived from the oversampled rate. Band
 * plan (crossovers by subtraction, bands sum back to the input):
 *   band 0 low : below 250 Hz        g 2.00, K 1.30, asym 0.30
 *   band 1 mid : the rest            g 1.15, K 0.60, asym 0.03
 *   band 2 high: 3.5-9 kHz           g 1.70, K 1.10, asym 0.06
 *   band 3 top : above 9 kHz         g 2.30, K 1.30, asym 0.06
 * Per band the shaper is (tanh(K*(g*x + a)) - tanh(K*a)) * N / g
 * with N = 1 / (K*(1 - tanh(K*a)^2)), which makes the small-signal
 * gain exactly 1: pre-emphasis in, complementary de-emphasis out,
 * net EQ ~0 dB on steady tones - only harmonics are added.
 * fma_sk_mB folds N / g into a single multiplier.
 */
function fma_silk_coef() (
  fma_sk_a1 = 1 - exp(-6.28318530717959 * 250 / SAMPLE_RATE);
  fma_sk_a2 = 1 - exp(-6.28318530717959 * 3500 / SAMPLE_RATE);
  fma_sk_a3 = 1 - exp(-6.28318530717959 * 9000 / SAMPLE_RATE);
  fma_sk_g0 = 2.0;  fma_sk_k0 = 1.3; fma_sk_o0 = 0.30;
  fma_sk_g1 = 1.15; fma_sk_k1 = 0.6; fma_sk_o1 = 0.03;
  fma_sk_g2 = 1.7;  fma_sk_k2 = 1.1; fma_sk_o2 = 0.06;
  fma_sk_g3 = 2.3;  fma_sk_k3 = 1.3; fma_sk_o3 = 0.06;
  fma_sk_t0 = fma_tanh(fma_sk_k0 * fma_sk_o0);
  fma_sk_t1 = fma_tanh(fma_sk_k1 * fma_sk_o1);
  fma_sk_t2 = fma_tanh(fma_sk_k2 * fma_sk_o2);
  fma_sk_t3 = fma_tanh(fma_sk_k3 * fma_sk_o3);
  fma_sk_m0 = 1 / (fma_sk_k0 * (1 - fma_sk_t0 * fma_sk_t0) * fma_sk_g0);
  fma_sk_m1 = 1 / (fma_sk_k1 * (1 - fma_sk_t1 * fma_sk_t1) * fma_sk_g1);
  fma_sk_m2 = 1 / (fma_sk_k2 * (1 - fma_sk_t2 * fma_sk_t2) * fma_sk_g2);
  fma_sk_m3 = 1 / (fma_sk_k3 * (1 - fma_sk_t3 * fma_sk_t3) * fma_sk_g3);
);

function set_oversample(os) local(fma_so_z) (
  // FMA fma.13 (Juan, 2026-10-21): HQ is x2 minimum-phase oversampling (the
  // Tukan/original ReEQ method) - zero-stuff, the SVF cascade runs at 2x,
  // then decimation through the generated Kaiser half-band (125 taps,
  // PDC 31). Active at every sample rate (no >= 88.2 kHz shutoff of the
  // original). os==0 is ECO.
  os ? (
    DO_OVERSAMPLE = 1;
    SAMPLE_RATE = srate * 2;
    ONE_OVER_SAMPLE_RATE = 1.0 / SAMPLE_RATE;
    pdc_delay = 31; // half-band center tap 62 at 2x = 31 base samples
    pdc_bot_ch = 0;
    pdc_top_ch = 2;
  ) : (
    DO_OVERSAMPLE = 0;
    SAMPLE_RATE = srate;
    ONE_OVER_SAMPLE_RATE = 1.0 / srate;
    pdc_delay = 0;
    pdc_bot_ch = 0;
    pdc_top_ch = 2;
  );
  fma_silk_coef();
  // On an actual mode change, clear the half-band histories so no stale
  // samples from a previous HQ visit leak into the output.
  (fma_os_prev != os && FMA_HB_HIST0 > 0) ? (
    fma_os_prev = os;
    fma_so_z = 0;
    while(fma_so_z < 128) (
      MEM[FMA_HB_HIST0 + fma_so_z] = 0;
      MEM[FMA_HB_HIST1 + fma_so_z] = 0;
      MEM[FMA_SK_H0 + fma_so_z] = 0;
      MEM[FMA_SK_H1 + fma_so_z] = 0;
      fma_so_z < 8 ? MEM[FMA_SK_ST + fma_so_z] = 0;
      fma_so_z += 1;
    );
  );
);

/*
 * FMA fma.13: the x2 half-band engine. The 125-tap Kaiser half-band is
 * generated by formula at @init (self-contained: no firhalfband import, no
 * per-rate tables). Design: A = 108 dB, beta = 0.1102 * (108 - 8.7).
 * 125 taps (not 127): the pair decimation scheme samples the even branch of
 * the 2x stream, so the center tap must sit on an even index (62) for the
 * flat identity to be exact and the delay an integer 31 base samples -
 * both verified by impulse render in the lab.
 */
function fma_i0(x) local(fma_i0_s, fma_i0_t, fma_i0_j, fma_i0_xq) (
  // Modified Bessel I0 by power series (init-time only).
  fma_i0_xq = x * x * 0.25;
  fma_i0_s = 1; fma_i0_t = 1; fma_i0_j = 1;
  while(fma_i0_j <= 60) (
    fma_i0_t *= fma_i0_xq / (fma_i0_j * fma_i0_j);
    fma_i0_s += fma_i0_t;
    fma_i0_t < 0.000000000000001 ? fma_i0_j = 1000 : fma_i0_j += 1;
  );
  fma_i0_s;
);

function fma_hb_gen() local(fma_hg_k, fma_hg_d, fma_hg_r, fma_hg_ideal,
    fma_hg_beta, fma_hg_i0b, fma_hg_g, fma_hg_nu, fma_hg_re) (
  fma_hg_beta = 10.9417; // Kaiser A = 108 dB
  fma_hg_i0b = fma_i0(fma_hg_beta);
  fma_hg_k = 0;
  while(fma_hg_k < 125) (
    fma_hg_d = fma_hg_k - 62;
    fma_hg_ideal = fma_hg_d == 0 ? 0.5 :
      sin(1.5707963267949 * fma_hg_d) / (3.14159265358979 * fma_hg_d);
    fma_hg_r = fma_hg_d / 62;
    MEM[FMA_HB_H + fma_hg_k] = fma_hg_ideal *
      fma_i0(fma_hg_beta * sqrt(max(0, 1 - fma_hg_r * fma_hg_r))) / fma_hg_i0b;
    fma_hg_k += 1;
  );
  // Display table: chain magnitude (dB) of the generated half-band over
  // nu = f / (2 * srate) in [0, 0.25], 257 points. The taps are symmetric,
  // so the response is real: R(nu) = h[62] + sum_pairs 2*h[k]*cos(...).
  // (Only odd k contribute; every even tap except the center is zero.)
  fma_hg_g = 0;
  while(fma_hg_g <= 256) (
    fma_hg_nu = 0.25 * fma_hg_g / 256;
    fma_hg_re = MEM[FMA_HB_H + 62];
    fma_hg_k = 1;
    while(fma_hg_k <= 61) (
      fma_hg_re += 2 * MEM[FMA_HB_H + fma_hg_k] *
        cos(6.28318530717959 * fma_hg_nu * (fma_hg_k - 62));
      fma_hg_k += 2;
    );
    MEM[FMA_HB_DISP + fma_hg_g] = 20 * log10(max(abs(fma_hg_re), 0.000000001));
    fma_hg_g += 1;
  );
);

// Pair-scheme half-band FIR: consumes the two 2x sub-samples (even, odd) of
// one base sample and returns the decimated output (x2 restores the energy
// of the zero-stuffed stream). base = channel history MEM base; the head
// index (next write slot) lives at MEM[base + 125].
function fma_hb_process(fma_hp_base, fma_hp_in0, fma_hp_in1)
  local(fma_hp_hp, fma_hp_acc, fma_hp_k, fma_hp_i1, fma_hp_i2, fma_hp_ic) (
  fma_hp_hp = MEM[fma_hp_base + 125];
  fma_hp_ic = fma_hp_hp - 62; fma_hp_ic < 0 ? fma_hp_ic += 125;
  fma_hp_acc = MEM[FMA_HB_H + 62] * MEM[fma_hp_base + fma_hp_ic];
  fma_hp_k = 1;
  while(fma_hp_k <= 61) (
    fma_hp_i1 = fma_hp_hp - fma_hp_k; fma_hp_i1 < 0 ? fma_hp_i1 += 125;
    fma_hp_i2 = fma_hp_hp - 124 + fma_hp_k; fma_hp_i2 < 0 ? fma_hp_i2 += 125;
    fma_hp_acc += MEM[FMA_HB_H + fma_hp_k] *
      (MEM[fma_hp_base + fma_hp_i1] + MEM[fma_hp_base + fma_hp_i2]);
    fma_hp_k += 2;
  );
  MEM[fma_hp_base + fma_hp_hp] = fma_hp_in0;
  fma_hp_hp += 1; fma_hp_hp >= 125 ? fma_hp_hp = 0;
  MEM[fma_hp_base + fma_hp_hp] = fma_hp_in1;
  fma_hp_hp += 1; fma_hp_hp >= 125 ? fma_hp_hp = 0;
  MEM[fma_hp_base + 125] = fma_hp_hp;
  2.0 * fma_hp_acc;
);

// Half-band chain magnitude (linear) at a display frequency, interpolated
// from the table generated with the taps.
function fma_hb_mag(freq) local(fma_hm_pos, fma_hm_i, fma_hm_fr, fma_hm_db) (
  fma_hm_pos = 512.0 * freq / srate;
  fma_hm_pos < 0 ? fma_hm_pos = 0;
  fma_hm_pos > 255.999 ? fma_hm_pos = 255.999;
  fma_hm_i = floor(fma_hm_pos);
  fma_hm_fr = fma_hm_pos - fma_hm_i;
  fma_hm_db = MEM[FMA_HB_DISP + fma_hm_i] * (1 - fma_hm_fr) +
              MEM[FMA_HB_DISP + fma_hm_i + 1] * fma_hm_fr;
  10 ^ (fma_hm_db / 20);
);

/*
 * FMA fma.19: full-rate lowpass of one 2x sub-sample position using
 * the generated half-band taps (MEM[FMA_HB_H]): the same symmetric
 * pairing fma_hb_process uses, evaluated around an arbitrary center
 * position of the 125-slot ring. Only odd taps are nonzero in a
 * half-band, so ~32 multiplies per position.
 */
function fma_silk_conv(fma_skc_base, fma_skc_c)
  local(fma_skc_k, fma_skc_acc, fma_skc_d, fma_skc_i1, fma_skc_i2) (
  fma_skc_acc = MEM[FMA_HB_H + 62] * MEM[fma_skc_base + fma_skc_c];
  fma_skc_k = 1;
  while (fma_skc_k <= 61) (
    fma_skc_d = 62 - fma_skc_k;
    fma_skc_i1 = fma_skc_c + fma_skc_d; fma_skc_i1 >= 125 ? fma_skc_i1 -= 125;
    fma_skc_i2 = fma_skc_c - fma_skc_d; fma_skc_i2 < 0 ? fma_skc_i2 += 125;
    fma_skc_acc += MEM[FMA_HB_H + fma_skc_k] * (MEM[fma_skc_base + fma_skc_i1] + MEM[fma_skc_base + fma_skc_i2]);
    fma_skc_k += 2;
  );
  fma_skc_acc;
);

/*
 * FMA fma.19: push one 2x pair into a channel's smoothing ring and
 * emit the half-band-lowpassed pair (globals fma_sk_sm0/fma_sk_sm1)
 * for the positions 62 sub-samples behind - linear phase, so the
 * pair stays phase-aligned inside the add path. The exciter works
 * on this image-free copy of the stream: the raw 2x stream still
 * carries the zero-stuff image (mirror content above the 1x
 * Nyquist) and a memoryless shaper would intermodulate the signal
 * with its own image (a 21.6 kHz tone at Silk 100 sprayed a spur
 * at 4.8 kHz only 39 dB down before this filter existed - now the
 * image is ~109 dB down at the shaper). The dry path is never
 * filtered: only the harmonic residue is delayed, and its own
 * fundamental cancels inside the residue, so the stage adds no
 * latency and no EQ of its own.
 */
function fma_silk_smooth(fma_sks_base, fma_sks_in0, fma_sks_in1)
  local(fma_sks_hp, fma_sks_e) (
  fma_sks_hp = MEM[fma_sks_base + 125];
  MEM[fma_sks_base + fma_sks_hp] = fma_sks_in0;
  fma_sks_hp += 1; fma_sks_hp >= 125 ? fma_sks_hp = 0;
  MEM[fma_sks_base + fma_sks_hp] = fma_sks_in1;
  fma_sks_hp += 1; fma_sks_hp >= 125 ? fma_sks_hp = 0;
  MEM[fma_sks_base + 125] = fma_sks_hp;
  fma_sks_e = fma_sks_hp - 64; fma_sks_e < 0 ? fma_sks_e += 125;
  fma_sk_sm0 = fma_silk_conv(fma_sks_base, fma_sks_e);
  fma_sks_e += 1; fma_sks_e >= 125 ? fma_sks_e -= 125;
  fma_sk_sm1 = fma_silk_conv(fma_sks_base, fma_sks_e);
);

/*
 * FMA fma.19: the Silk spectral exciter's residue for one smoothed
 * 2x sub-sample. Band states live in MEM at fma_sk_base + 0..2
 * (one-pole states for the 250 Hz low split, the 3.5 kHz high
 * split and the 9 kHz top split). The four bands sum back to the
 * input exactly and each shaper has unity small-signal gain, so
 * the return value is pure harmonic residue (~0 for quiet
 * material); the caller mixes amt * residue under the dry signal.
 */
function fma_silk_res(fma_sk_x, fma_sk_base)
  local(fma_sk_s, fma_sk_lo, fma_sk_hp, fma_sk_hi, fma_sk_top, fma_sk_mid, fma_sk_acc) (
  fma_sk_s = MEM[fma_sk_base];
  fma_sk_s += fma_sk_a1 * (fma_sk_x - fma_sk_s);
  MEM[fma_sk_base] = fma_sk_s;
  fma_sk_lo = fma_sk_s;
  fma_sk_s = MEM[fma_sk_base + 1];
  fma_sk_s += fma_sk_a2 * (fma_sk_x - fma_sk_s);
  MEM[fma_sk_base + 1] = fma_sk_s;
  fma_sk_hp = fma_sk_x - fma_sk_s;
  fma_sk_s = MEM[fma_sk_base + 2];
  fma_sk_s += fma_sk_a3 * (fma_sk_hp - fma_sk_s);
  MEM[fma_sk_base + 2] = fma_sk_s;
  fma_sk_hi = fma_sk_s;
  fma_sk_top = fma_sk_hp - fma_sk_s;
  fma_sk_mid = fma_sk_x - fma_sk_lo - fma_sk_hi - fma_sk_top;
  fma_sk_acc = (fma_tanh(fma_sk_k0 * (fma_sk_g0 * fma_sk_lo + fma_sk_o0)) - fma_sk_t0) * fma_sk_m0 - fma_sk_lo;
  fma_sk_acc += (fma_tanh(fma_sk_k1 * (fma_sk_g1 * fma_sk_mid + fma_sk_o1)) - fma_sk_t1) * fma_sk_m1 - fma_sk_mid;
  fma_sk_acc += (fma_tanh(fma_sk_k2 * (fma_sk_g2 * fma_sk_hi + fma_sk_o2)) - fma_sk_t2) * fma_sk_m2 - fma_sk_hi;
  fma_sk_acc += (fma_tanh(fma_sk_k3 * (fma_sk_g3 * fma_sk_top + fma_sk_o3)) - fma_sk_t3) * fma_sk_m3 - fma_sk_top;
  fma_sk_acc;
);

/*
 * FMA fma.19: the finished limiter law - soft ceiling at -1 dBFS
 * (0.8912509). Bit-exact passthrough at and below the -3 dBFS knee
 * (0.7079458); above it, K + D*tanh((|x|-K)/D) with D = T - K:
 * slope 1 at the knee (C1), monotone, asymptotic to the ceiling,
 * and the final min() guarantees the ceiling is never exceeded.
 * No memory, no latency.
 */
function fma_softceil(fma_sc_x) local(fma_sc_ax, fma_sc_y) (
  fma_sc_ax = abs(fma_sc_x);
  fma_sc_ax <= 0.7079458 ? fma_sc_x : (
    fma_sc_y = 0.7079458 + 0.1833051 * fma_tanh((fma_sc_ax - 0.7079458) / 0.1833051);
    (fma_sc_x < 0 ? -1 : 1) * min(fma_sc_y, 0.8912509);
  );
);


/*
 * Update the state of any changes
 */
function update_state() local (blocks, fade, fill_r, fill_g, fill_b, fill_a, line_r, line_g, line_b, line_a) (
  spectrum.ceiling = Ceiling_Value == 0 ? 0 : Ceiling_Value == 1 ? 20 : Ceiling_Value == 2 ? 40;
  spectrum.noise_floor = Floor_Value == 0 ? -90 : Floor_Value == 1 ? -140 : Floor_Value == 2 ? -200;
  spectrum.tilt = Tilt_Value == 0 ? 0 : Tilt_Value == 1 ? 1.5 : Tilt_Value == 2 ? 3 : Tilt_Value == 3 ? 4.5 :
                  Tilt_Value == 4 ? 6;

  spectrum.windowtype != Type_Value+1 ? spectrum.set_type(Type_Value+1);

  blocks = (2 ^ (Block_Value+1)) * 1024;

  spectrum.windowsize != blocks ? spectrum.set_block_size(blocks);

  fade = do_listen ? 0.5 : 1.0;

  // Listen spectrum colours
  listline_r = (240 / 255) * 0.80;
  listline_g = (101 / 255) * 0.80;
  listline_b = (76 / 255) * 0.80;

  Display_Mode == 0 ? (
    fill_r = 46 / 255;
    fill_g = 71 / 255;
    fill_b = 83 / 255;
    fill_a = 1.0;
    spectrum.set_fill(0, 1);
    spectrum.set_color(0, fill_r*fade, fill_g*fade, fill_b*fade, fill_a);

    spectrum.set_fill(2, 0);
    spectrum.set_color(2, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 1);

    fill_r = 96 / 255;
    fill_g = 223 / 255;
    fill_b = 255 / 255;
    fill_a = 0.5;
    spectrum.set_fill(1, 1); 
    spectrum.set_color(1, fill_r*fade, fill_g*fade, fill_b*fade, fill_a);

    spectrum.set_fill(3, 0);
    spectrum.set_color(3, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 1);

    spectrum.set_fill(4, 0);
    spectrum.set_color(4, listline_r, listline_g, listline_b, 1);

    spectrum.set_fill(5, 0);
    spectrum.set_color(5, listline_r*0.80, listline_g*0.80, listline_b*0.80, 1);

  ) : Display_Mode == 1 ? (
    line_a=1.0;
    line_r = 114 / 255; line_g = 215 / 255; line_b = 253 / 255;;
    spectrum.set_fill(0, 0);
    spectrum.set_color(0, line_r*fade, line_g*fade, line_b*fade, line_a);
    
    spectrum.set_fill(2, 0);
    spectrum.set_color(2, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 1);

    line_r = 253 / 255; line_g = 185 / 255; line_b = 21 / 255;;
    spectrum.set_fill(1, 0);
    spectrum.set_color(1, line_r*fade, line_g*fade, line_b*fade, line_a);

    spectrum.set_fill(3, 0);
    spectrum.set_color(3, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 1);

    spectrum.set_fill(4, 0);
    spectrum.set_color(4, listline_r, listline_g, listline_b, 1);

    spectrum.set_fill(5, 0);
    spectrum.set_color(5, listline_r*0.80, listline_g*0.80, listline_b*0.80, 1);
  );

  Db_Range == 0 ? (DB_EQ_RANGE = 6; DB_EQ_RANGE_STEPS = 1;) : 
    Db_Range == 1 ? (DB_EQ_RANGE = 12; DB_EQ_RANGE_STEPS = 3;) :
      Db_Range == 2 ? (DB_EQ_RANGE = 18; DB_EQ_RANGE_STEPS = 6;) :
        Db_Range == 3 ? (DB_EQ_RANGE = 24; DB_EQ_RANGE_STEPS = 8;) :
          Db_Range == 4 ? (DB_EQ_RANGE = 30; DB_EQ_RANGE_STEPS = 10;);
);

/*
 * Notify Reaper that frequency has been touched
 */
function notify_touched_frequency(node) (
  // Notify Reaper that a parameter change has happened
  node == 0 ? slider_automate(Node1_Frequency) :
    node == 1 ? slider_automate(Node2_Frequency) :
      node == 2 ? slider_automate(Node3_Frequency) :
        node == 3 ? slider_automate(Node4_Frequency) :
          node == 4 ? slider_automate(Node5_Frequency);
);

/*
 * Notify Reaper that gain has been touched
 */
function notify_touched_gain(node) (
  // Notify Reaper that a parameter change has happened
  node == 0 ? slider_automate(Node1_Gain) :
    node == 1 ? slider_automate(Node2_Gain) :
      node == 2 ? slider_automate(Node3_Gain) :
        node == 3 ? slider_automate(Node4_Gain) :
          node == 4 ? slider_automate(Node5_Gain);
);

/*
 * Notify Reaper that Q has been touched
 */
function notify_touched_Q(node) (
  // Notify Reaper that a parameter change has happened
  node == 0 ? slider_automate(Node1_Q) :
    node == 1 ? slider_automate(Node2_Q) :
      node == 2 ? slider_automate(Node3_Q) :
        node == 3 ? slider_automate(Node4_Q) :
          node == 4 ? slider_automate(Node5_Q);
);

function band_init()
  instance (enabled, type, frequency, gain, q, filter, color) ( 
  filter.svf_set_sample_rate(SAMPLE_RATE);
  filter.svf_bypass();
  color.create_color(0,0,0);

  filter.a1 = filter.t_a1;
  filter.a2 = filter.t_a2;
  filter.a3 = filter.t_a3;

  filter.m0 = filter.t_m0;
  filter.m1 = filter.t_m1;
  filter.m2 = filter.t_m2;
  filter.iter_t = 1.0;
);

/*
 * Set the filter
 */
function band_set_filter(t, f, g, qval, slope)
  instance (enabled, type, frequency, gain, q, filter, color) (
  type = t; frequency = f; gain = g; q = qval;
  type == 0 ? filter.svf_eq(frequency, q, db_to_gain(gain)) :
    type == 1 ? filter.svf_hp(frequency, q, slope) :
      type == 2 ? filter.svf_hpb(frequency, slope) :
        type == 3 ? filter.svf_ls(frequency, q, db_to_gain(gain)) :
          type == 4 ? filter.svf_hs(frequency, q, db_to_gain(gain)) :
            type == 5 ? filter.svf_lp(frequency, q, slope) :
              type == 6 ? filter.svf_lpb(frequency, slope) :
                type == 7 ? filter.svf_bs(frequency, q) :
                  type == 8 ? filter.svf_bp2(frequency, q) :
                    type == 9 ? filter.svf_st(frequency, q, gain) :
                      type == 10 ? filter.svf_pultecls(frequency, q, gain) :
                        type == 11 ? filter.svf_ap(frequency, q) :
                          type == 12 ? filter.svf_analog_lowcut(frequency, q, gain) :
                            type == 13 ? filter.svf_analog_highcut(frequency, q, gain);
);

/*
 * Convert slider % to frequency
 */
function per_to_freq(x, range) (
  MIN_FREQ * exp(FREQ_LOG_MAX * x / range);
);

/*
 * Convert frequency to slider %
 */
function freq_to_per(freq, range) (
  range * log(freq / MIN_FREQ) / FREQ_LOG_MAX;
);


function per_to_q(x, range) (
  MIN_Q * exp(Q_LOG_MAX * x / range);
);

/*
 * Convert frequency to slider %
 */
function q_to_per(q, range) (
  range * log(q / MIN_Q) / Q_LOG_MAX;
);


/*
 * Update sliders with filter data
 */
function filters_to_sliders() ( 
  Node1_Enabled = Band_Enabled[0];
  Node1_Group = Band_Group[0];
  Node1_Type = Band_Type[0];
  Node1_Frequency = freq_to_per(Band_Frequency[0], 100);
  Node1_Gain = Band_Gain[0];
  Node1_Q = q_to_per(Band_Q[0], 100);
  Node1_Slope = Band_Slope[0];

  Node2_Enabled = Band_Enabled[1];
  Node2_Group = Band_Group[1];
  Node2_Type = Band_Type[1];
  Node2_Frequency = freq_to_per(Band_Frequency[1], 100);
  Node2_Gain = Band_Gain[1];
  Node2_Q = q_to_per(Band_Q[1], 100);
  Node2_Slope = Band_Slope[1];

  Node3_Enabled = Band_Enabled[2];
  Node3_Group = Band_Group[2];
  Node3_Type = Band_Type[2];
  Node3_Frequency = freq_to_per(Band_Frequency[2], 100);
  Node3_Gain = Band_Gain[2];
  Node3_Q = q_to_per(Band_Q[2], 100);
  Node3_Slope = Band_Slope[2];

  Node4_Enabled = Band_Enabled[3];
  Node4_Group = Band_Group[3];
  Node4_Type = Band_Type[3];
  Node4_Frequency = freq_to_per(Band_Frequency[3], 100);
  Node4_Gain = Band_Gain[3];
  Node4_Q = q_to_per(Band_Q[3], 100);
  Node4_Slope = Band_Slope[3];

  Node5_Enabled = Band_Enabled[4];
  Node5_Group = Band_Group[4];
  Node5_Type = Band_Type[4];
  Node5_Frequency = freq_to_per(Band_Frequency[4], 100);
  Node5_Gain = Band_Gain[4];
  Node5_Q = q_to_per(Band_Q[4], 100);
  Node5_Slope = Band_Slope[4];
);

/*
 * Update filter data with sliders
 */
function sliders_to_filters() ( 
  Band_Enabled[0] = Node1_Enabled;
  Band_Group[0] = Node1_Group;
  Band_Type[0] = Node1_Type;
  Band_Frequency[0] = per_to_freq(Node1_Frequency, 100);
  Band_Gain[0] = Node1_Gain;
  Band_Q[0] = per_to_q(Node1_Q, 100);
  Band_Slope[0] = Node1_Slope;

  Band_Enabled[1] = Node2_Enabled;
  Band_Group[1] = Node2_Group;
  Band_Type[1] = Node2_Type;
  Band_Frequency[1] = per_to_freq(Node2_Frequency, 100);
  Band_Gain[1] = Node2_Gain;
  Band_Q[1] = per_to_q(Node2_Q, 100);
  Band_Slope[1] = Node2_Slope;

  Band_Enabled[2] = Node3_Enabled;
  Band_Group[2] = Node3_Group;
  Band_Type[2] = Node3_Type;
  Band_Frequency[2] = per_to_freq(Node3_Frequency, 100);;
  Band_Gain[2] = Node3_Gain;
  Band_Q[2] = per_to_q(Node3_Q, 100);
  Band_Slope[2] = Node3_Slope;

  Band_Enabled[3] = Node4_Enabled;
  Band_Group[3] = Node4_Group;
  Band_Type[3] = Node4_Type;
  Band_Frequency[3] = per_to_freq(Node4_Frequency, 100);;
  Band_Gain[3] = Node4_Gain;
  Band_Q[3] = per_to_q(Node4_Q, 100);
  Band_Slope[3] = Node4_Slope;

  Band_Enabled[4] = Node5_Enabled;
  Band_Group[4] = Node5_Group;
  Band_Type[4] = Node5_Type;
  Band_Frequency[4] = per_to_freq(Node5_Frequency, 100);;
  Band_Gain[4] = Node5_Gain;
  Band_Q[4] = per_to_q(Node5_Q, 100);
  Band_Slope[4] = Node5_Slope;
);

/*
 * Flag filter to update for both audio and graphics
 */
function flag_filter_update(band) ( 
  DynForce[band] = 1;
  Band_Update[band] = 1;
  Band_GfxUpdate[band] = 1;
 );

function flag_filter_update_all() ( 
  Band_Update[0] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[0] = 1;
  Band_Update[1] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[1] = 1;
  Band_Update[2] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[2] = 1;
  Band_Update[3] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[3] = 1;
  Band_Update[4] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[4] = 1;
  Band_Update[5] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[5] = 1;
  Band_Update[6] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[6] = 1;
  Band_Update[7] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[7] = 1;
  Band_Update[8] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[8] = 1;
  Band_Update[9] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[9] = 1;
  Band_Update[10] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[10] = 1;
  Band_Update[11] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[11] = 1;
  Band_Update[12] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[12] = 1;
  Band_Update[13] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[13] = 1;
  Band_Update[14] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[14] = 1;
  Band_Update[15] = 1; Band_GfxUpdate[15] = 1;
  fma_tmp_i = 0;
  while(fma_tmp_i < 16) (
    DynForce[fma_tmp_i] = 1;
    fma_tmp_i += 1;
  );
 );

/*
 * Update the filter parameters
 */
function update_visual_filters() local (band_scalar) (
  band_scalar = Scale / 100.0;

  Band_GfxUpdate[0] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[0] = 0; gfx_band1.band_set_filter(Band_Type[0], Band_Frequency[0], Band_Gain[0] * band_scalar, Band_Q[0], Band_Slope[0]); gfx_band1.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[1] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[1] = 0; gfx_band2.band_set_filter(Band_Type[1], Band_Frequency[1], Band_Gain[1] * band_scalar, Band_Q[1], Band_Slope[1]); gfx_band2.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[2] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[2] = 0; gfx_band3.band_set_filter(Band_Type[2], Band_Frequency[2], Band_Gain[2] * band_scalar, Band_Q[2], Band_Slope[2]); gfx_band3.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[3] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[3] = 0; gfx_band4.band_set_filter(Band_Type[3], Band_Frequency[3], Band_Gain[3] * band_scalar, Band_Q[3], Band_Slope[3]); gfx_band4.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[4] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[4] = 0; gfx_band5.band_set_filter(Band_Type[4], Band_Frequency[4], Band_Gain[4] * band_scalar, Band_Q[4], Band_Slope[4]); gfx_band5.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[5] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[5] = 0; gfx_band6.band_set_filter(Band_Type[5], Band_Frequency[5], Band_Gain[5] * band_scalar, Band_Q[5], Band_Slope[5]); gfx_band6.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[6] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[6] = 0; gfx_band7.band_set_filter(Band_Type[6], Band_Frequency[6], Band_Gain[6] * band_scalar, Band_Q[6], Band_Slope[6]); gfx_band7.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[7] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[7] = 0; gfx_band8.band_set_filter(Band_Type[7], Band_Frequency[7], Band_Gain[7] * band_scalar, Band_Q[7], Band_Slope[7]); gfx_band8.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[8] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[8] = 0; gfx_band9.band_set_filter(Band_Type[8], Band_Frequency[8], Band_Gain[8] * band_scalar, Band_Q[8], Band_Slope[8]); gfx_band9.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[9] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[9] = 0; gfx_band10.band_set_filter(Band_Type[9], Band_Frequency[9], Band_Gain[9] * band_scalar, Band_Q[9], Band_Slope[9]); gfx_band10.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[10] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[10] = 0; gfx_band11.band_set_filter(Band_Type[10], Band_Frequency[10], Band_Gain[10] * band_scalar, Band_Q[10], Band_Slope[10]); gfx_band11.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[11] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[11] = 0; gfx_band12.band_set_filter(Band_Type[11], Band_Frequency[11], Band_Gain[11] * band_scalar, Band_Q[11], Band_Slope[11]); gfx_band12.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[12] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[12] = 0; gfx_band13.band_set_filter(Band_Type[12], Band_Frequency[12], Band_Gain[12] * band_scalar, Band_Q[12], Band_Slope[12]); gfx_band13.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[13] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[13] = 0; gfx_band14.band_set_filter(Band_Type[13], Band_Frequency[13], Band_Gain[13] * band_scalar, Band_Q[13], Band_Slope[13]); gfx_band14.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[14] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[14] = 0; gfx_band15.band_set_filter(Band_Type[14], Band_Frequency[14], Band_Gain[14] * band_scalar, Band_Q[14], Band_Slope[14]); gfx_band15.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
  Band_GfxUpdate[15] ? (Band_GfxUpdate[15] = 0; gfx_band16.band_set_filter(Band_Type[15], Band_Frequency[15], Band_Gain[15] * band_scalar, Band_Q[15], Band_Slope[15]); gfx_band16.filter.svf_set_to_target(); );
);

function update_audio_filters() local (band_scalar) (
  band_scalar = Scale / 100.0;

  Band_Update[0] ? (Band_Update[0] = 0; Band_Enabled[0] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band1.filter.svf_bypass() : band1.band_set_filter(Band_Type[0], Band_Frequency[0], Band_Gain[0] * band_scalar, Band_Q[0], Band_Slope[0]); );
  Band_Update[1] ? (Band_Update[1] = 0; Band_Enabled[1] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band2.filter.svf_bypass() : band2.band_set_filter(Band_Type[1], Band_Frequency[1], Band_Gain[1] * band_scalar, Band_Q[1], Band_Slope[1]); );
  Band_Update[2] ? (Band_Update[2] = 0; Band_Enabled[2] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band3.filter.svf_bypass() : band3.band_set_filter(Band_Type[2], Band_Frequency[2], Band_Gain[2] * band_scalar, Band_Q[2], Band_Slope[2]); );
  Band_Update[3] ? (Band_Update[3] = 0; Band_Enabled[3] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band4.filter.svf_bypass() : band4.band_set_filter(Band_Type[3], Band_Frequency[3], Band_Gain[3] * band_scalar, Band_Q[3], Band_Slope[3]); );
  Band_Update[4] ? (Band_Update[4] = 0; Band_Enabled[4] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band5.filter.svf_bypass() : band5.band_set_filter(Band_Type[4], Band_Frequency[4], Band_Gain[4] * band_scalar, Band_Q[4], Band_Slope[4]); );
  Band_Update[5] ? (Band_Update[5] = 0; Band_Enabled[5] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band6.filter.svf_bypass() : band6.band_set_filter(Band_Type[5], Band_Frequency[5], Band_Gain[5] * band_scalar, Band_Q[5], Band_Slope[5]); );
  Band_Update[6] ? (Band_Update[6] = 0; Band_Enabled[6] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band7.filter.svf_bypass() : band7.band_set_filter(Band_Type[6], Band_Frequency[6], Band_Gain[6] * band_scalar, Band_Q[6], Band_Slope[6]); );
  Band_Update[7] ? (Band_Update[7] = 0; Band_Enabled[7] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band8.filter.svf_bypass() : band8.band_set_filter(Band_Type[7], Band_Frequency[7], Band_Gain[7] * band_scalar, Band_Q[7], Band_Slope[7]); );
  Band_Update[8] ? (Band_Update[8] = 0; Band_Enabled[8] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band9.filter.svf_bypass() : band9.band_set_filter(Band_Type[8], Band_Frequency[8], Band_Gain[8] * band_scalar, Band_Q[8], Band_Slope[8]); );
  Band_Update[9] ? (Band_Update[9] = 0; Band_Enabled[9] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band10.filter.svf_bypass() : band10.band_set_filter(Band_Type[9], Band_Frequency[9], Band_Gain[9] * band_scalar, Band_Q[9], Band_Slope[9]); );
  Band_Update[10] ? (Band_Update[10] = 0; Band_Enabled[10] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band11.filter.svf_bypass() : band11.band_set_filter(Band_Type[10], Band_Frequency[10], Band_Gain[10] * band_scalar, Band_Q[10], Band_Slope[10]); );
  Band_Update[11] ? (Band_Update[11] = 0; Band_Enabled[11] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band12.filter.svf_bypass() : band12.band_set_filter(Band_Type[11], Band_Frequency[11], Band_Gain[11] * band_scalar, Band_Q[11], Band_Slope[11]); );
  Band_Update[12] ? (Band_Update[12] = 0; Band_Enabled[12] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band13.filter.svf_bypass() : band13.band_set_filter(Band_Type[12], Band_Frequency[12], Band_Gain[12] * band_scalar, Band_Q[12], Band_Slope[12]); );
  Band_Update[13] ? (Band_Update[13] = 0; Band_Enabled[13] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band14.filter.svf_bypass() : band14.band_set_filter(Band_Type[13], Band_Frequency[13], Band_Gain[13] * band_scalar, Band_Q[13], Band_Slope[13]); );
  Band_Update[14] ? (Band_Update[14] = 0; Band_Enabled[14] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band15.filter.svf_bypass() : band15.band_set_filter(Band_Type[14], Band_Frequency[14], Band_Gain[14] * band_scalar, Band_Q[14], Band_Slope[14]); );
  Band_Update[15] ? (Band_Update[15] = 0; Band_Enabled[15] != BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? band16.filter.svf_bypass() : band16.band_set_filter(Band_Type[15], Band_Frequency[15], Band_Gain[15] * band_scalar, Band_Q[15], Band_Slope[15]); );
);

/*
 * FMA Etapa 2: per-band dynamics.
 * RBJ bandpass (constant 0 dB peak gain) at the band's own freq/Q.
 */
function fma_det_coeffs(i) local (w0, cw, sw, alpha, a0) (
  w0 = 6.28318530717959 * Band_Frequency[i] / srate;
  cw = cos(w0); sw = sin(w0);
  alpha = sw / (2 * max(Band_Q[i], 0.05));
  a0 = 1 + alpha;
  DetB0[i] = alpha / a0;
  DetB1[i] = 0;
  DetB2[i] = -alpha / a0;
  DetA1[i] = -2 * cw / a0;
  DetA2[i] = (1 - alpha) / a0;
);

/* FMA Etapa 2.1: per-band detector envelope coefficients from the band's
 * ATTACK/RELEASE dials (ms). Called at init, on srate change, and whenever
 * DynForce is set (ATK/REL edits). */
function fma_det_env_coeffs(i) (
  DetAtk[i] = 1 - exp(-1 / (max(Band_Dyn_Atk[i], 0.5) * 0.001 * srate));
  DetRel[i] = 1 - exp(-1 / (max(Band_Dyn_Rel[i], 1) * 0.001 * srate));
);

/* FMA Etapa 2: apply static gain x scale + current dynamic offset to band i */
function fma_dyn_set(i, bsc) (
  i == 0 ? band1.band_set_filter(Band_Type[0], Band_Frequency[0], Band_Gain[0]*bsc + DynApplied[0], Band_Q[0], Band_Slope[0]) :
  i == 1 ? band2.band_set_filter(Band_Type[1], Band_Frequency[1], Band_Gain[1]*bsc + DynApplied[1], Band_Q[1], Band_Slope[1]) :
  i == 2 ? band3.band_set_filter(Band_Type[2], Band_Frequency[2], Band_Gain[2]*bsc + DynApplied[2], Band_Q[2], Band_Slope[2]) :
  i == 3 ? band4.band_set_filter(Band_Type[3], Band_Frequency[3], Band_Gain[3]*bsc + DynApplied[3], Band_Q[3], Band_Slope[3]) :
  i == 4 ? band5.band_set_filter(Band_Type[4], Band_Frequency[4], Band_Gain[4]*bsc + DynApplied[4], Band_Q[4], Band_Slope[4]) :
  i == 5 ? band6.band_set_filter(Band_Type[5], Band_Frequency[5], Band_Gain[5]*bsc + DynApplied[5], Band_Q[5], Band_Slope[5]) :
  i == 6 ? band7.band_set_filter(Band_Type[6], Band_Frequency[6], Band_Gain[6]*bsc + DynApplied[6], Band_Q[6], Band_Slope[6]) :
  i == 7 ? band8.band_set_filter(Band_Type[7], Band_Frequency[7], Band_Gain[7]*bsc + DynApplied[7], Band_Q[7], Band_Slope[7]) :
  i == 8 ? band9.band_set_filter(Band_Type[8], Band_Frequency[8], Band_Gain[8]*bsc + DynApplied[8], Band_Q[8], Band_Slope[8]) :
  i == 9 ? band10.band_set_filter(Band_Type[9], Band_Frequency[9], Band_Gain[9]*bsc + DynApplied[9], Band_Q[9], Band_Slope[9]) :
  i == 10 ? band11.band_set_filter(Band_Type[10], Band_Frequency[10], Band_Gain[10]*bsc + DynApplied[10], Band_Q[10], Band_Slope[10]) :
  i == 11 ? band12.band_set_filter(Band_Type[11], Band_Frequency[11], Band_Gain[11]*bsc + DynApplied[11], Band_Q[11], Band_Slope[11]) :
  i == 12 ? band13.band_set_filter(Band_Type[12], Band_Frequency[12], Band_Gain[12]*bsc + DynApplied[12], Band_Q[12], Band_Slope[12]) :
  i == 13 ? band14.band_set_filter(Band_Type[13], Band_Frequency[13], Band_Gain[13]*bsc + DynApplied[13], Band_Q[13], Band_Slope[13]) :
  i == 14 ? band15.band_set_filter(Band_Type[14], Band_Frequency[14], Band_Gain[14]*bsc + DynApplied[14], Band_Q[14], Band_Slope[14]) :
  i == 15 ? band16.band_set_filter(Band_Type[15], Band_Frequency[15], Band_Gain[15]*bsc + DynApplied[15], Band_Q[15], Band_Slope[15]) :
  0;
);



/* FMA Etapa 2.1: node menu Dynamic on/off toggle - flips the per-band
 * Band_DynOn flag (same state as the panel's DYN ON/OFF button). The DYN
 * knob value is preserved while off; new bands default to OFF. */
function fma_dyn_menu_toggle(b) (
  Band_DynOn[b] = Band_DynOn[b] ? 0 : 1;
  DynForce[b] = 1;
);

/*
 * FMA Etapa 2: apply the Dynamic toggle to all selected nodes (same convention
 * as toggle_nodes_enabled).
 */
function dyn_toggle_selected_nodes(band) local(i) (
  i = 0;
  while(i < NUM_BANDS) (
    Band_Selected[i] ? fma_dyn_menu_toggle(i);
    i += 1;
  );
  filters_to_sliders();
);


/*
 * FMA Etapa 2: per-block maintenance - dynamics detector bookkeeping.
 * Called once per @block.
 */
function fma_block_maintain() local (band_scalar, i, rng, e, lev, over, dyn) (
  band_scalar = Scale / 100.0;
  fma_dyn_armed = 0;
  i = 0;
  while(i < 16) (
    rng = Band_Dynamic_Range[i];
    Band_DynOn[i] && rng != 0 && Band_Enabled[i] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED ? (
      fma_dyn_armed = 1;
      Band_DynArmed[i] = 1;
      DynForce[i] ? ( fma_det_coeffs(i); fma_det_env_coeffs(i); );
      e = DetEnv[i];
      lev = 8.68588963806504 * log(e + 0.000000001);
      over = lev - Band_Dynamic_Thr[i]; over < 0 ? over = 0;
      dyn = over * (rng / 24);
      dyn > 24 ? dyn = 24; dyn < -24 ? dyn = -24;
      (DynForce[i] || abs(dyn - DynApplied[i]) > 0.004) ? (
        DynApplied[i] = dyn; DynForce[i] = 0;
        fma_dyn_set(i, band_scalar);
      );
    ) : (
      Band_DynArmed[i] = 0;
      DynApplied[i] != 0 ? (
        DynApplied[i] = 0; fma_dyn_set(i, band_scalar);
      );
      DynForce[i] = 0;
    );
    i += 1;
  );
);

init_rate != srate ? (
  init_rate = srate;

  // Initialise everything

  MEMORY.init_memory();

  spectrum.init();

  MEMORY.index = spectrum.get_memory_index();

  BAND_STATE_OFF = 0;
  BAND_STATE_DISABLED = 1;
  BAND_STATE_ENABLED = 2;
  BAND_STATE_INFORM_DISABLE = 3;

  // Allocate and init filter bands
  NUM_BANDS = 16;

  Band_Update = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_GfxUpdate = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Enabled = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Group = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Type = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Frequency = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Gain = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Q = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Slope = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Dynamic_Range = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Red = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Green = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Blue = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);

  Band_Selected = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Drag_OffsetX = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Drag_OffsetY = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Invert_dB = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Selected_States = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  // FMA Etapa 2: per-band dynamics state (Band_Dynamic_Range already existed)
  Band_Dynamic_Thr = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Dyn_Atk = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_Dyn_Rel = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  Band_DynArmed = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DynForce = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DynApplied = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetEnv = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetB0 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetB1 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetB2 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetA1 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetA2 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetX1 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetX2 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetY1 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetY2 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  // FMA fma.13: x2 half-band state - generated Kaiser taps (125), per-channel
  // circular histories (125 samples + head slot), display response table
  FMA_HB_H = MEMORY.alloc_memory(125);
  FMA_HB_HIST0 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(128);
  FMA_HB_HIST1 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(128);
  FMA_HB_DISP = MEMORY.alloc_memory(257);
  FMA_SK_ST = MEMORY.alloc_memory(8); // FMA fma.19: Silk band states (2 ch x 3 one-pole states, stride 4)
  FMA_SK_H0 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(128); // FMA fma.19: Silk add-path smoothing ring L (125 taps + head)
  FMA_SK_H1 = MEMORY.alloc_memory(128); // FMA fma.19: Silk add-path smoothing ring R
  // FMA Etapa 2.3: dynamics viz - one static-curve Y column per 2 px,
  // up to 4096 px graph width (gfx thread only)
  FMA23_VY = MEMORY.alloc_memory(2048);
  // FMA Etapa 2.1: per-band dynamics on/off + per-band envelope coefficients
  Band_DynOn = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetAtk = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  DetRel = MEMORY.alloc_memory(NUM_BANDS);
  QualityModes = MEMORY.alloc_memory(3);
  QualityModesMenu = MEMORY.alloc_memory(3);
  band = 0;
  while (band < NUM_BANDS) (
    Band_Selected[band] = 0;
    Band_Drag_OffsetX[band] = 0;
    Band_Drag_OffsetY[band] = 0;
    Band_Invert_dB[band] = 0;
    Band_Selected_States[band] = 0;
    Band_Dynamic_Thr[band] = -24;
    Band_Dyn_Atk[band] = 10;
    Band_Dyn_Rel[band] = 100;
    Band_DynOn[band] = 0; // FMA Etapa 2.1: new bands start with dynamics OFF
    band += 1;
  );

  // FMA fma.13: generate the Kaiser half-band taps and the display table
  // from them (formula-generated at load; valid at any sample rate).
  fma_hb_gen();

  QualityModesMenu[0] = "ECO";
  QualityModesMenu[1] = "HQ";

  // FMA Etapa 2.1: per-band detector envelope coefficients from
  // Band_Dyn_Atk/Band_Dyn_Rel (ms); recomputed on srate change and on
  // ATK/REL edits via fma_det_env_coeffs()
  fma_tmp_b = 0;
  while(fma_tmp_b < NUM_BANDS) (
    fma_det_env_coeffs(fma_tmp_b);
    fma_tmp_b += 1;
  );

  // FMA fma.13: oversampling state. DO_OVERSAMPLE is (re)set by
  // set_oversample() below; a fresh instance always starts in ECO
  // (Quality slider default 0).
  DO_OVERSAMPLE = 0;
  fma_os_prev = 0;
  fma_dyn_armed = 0;

  band_selected_circle_last_time = time_precise();
  band_selected_circle_phase = 0.0;
  band_selected_circle_alpha = 0.8;

  // Filters for @slider, @block and @sample
  band1.band_init();
  band2.band_init();
  band3.band_init();
  band4.band_init();
  band5.band_init();
  band6.band_init();
  band7.band_init();
  band8.band_init();
  band9.band_init();
  band10.band_init();
  band11.band_init();
  band12.band_init();
  band13.band_init();
  band14.band_init();
  band15.band_init();
  band16.band_init();

  // Filters for @gfx
  gfx_band1.band_init();
  gfx_band2.band_init();
  gfx_band3.band_init();
  gfx_band4.band_init();
  gfx_band5.band_init();
  gfx_band6.band_init();
  gfx_band7.band_init();
  gfx_band8.band_init();
  gfx_band9.band_init();
  gfx_band10.band_init();
  gfx_band11.band_init();
  gfx_band12.band_init();
  gfx_band13.band_init();
  gfx_band14.band_init();
  gfx_band15.band_init();
  gfx_band16.band_init();

  color_band0.create_color(231, 33, 75);
  color_band1.create_color(241, 111, 50);
  color_band2.create_color(253, 199, 50);
  color_band3.create_color(126, 188, 111);
  color_band4.create_color(20, 146, 104);
  color_band5.create_color(19, 124, 168);
  color_band6.create_color(48, 57, 142);
  color_band7.create_color(135, 45, 138);
  color_band8.create_color(231, 33, 75);
  color_band9.create_color(241, 111, 50);
  color_band10.create_color(253, 199, 50);
  color_band11.create_color(126, 188, 111);
  color_band12.create_color(20, 146, 104);
  color_band13.create_color(19, 124, 168);
  color_band14.create_color(48, 57, 142);
  color_band15.create_color(135, 45, 138);

  // FMA fma.11: the HQ x8 half-band engine was removed (Juan, 2026-10-19)
  // and HQ became the Linear Phase engine; fma.13 removes that engine
  // too - HQ is now x2 minimum-phase oversampling (see set_oversample).

  // Allocate and init RMS
  rms_time_constant_ms = 300;
  rms_alloc = (0.001 * rms_time_constant_ms * 192000)|0;
  rms_max_count = (0.001 * rms_time_constant_ms * srate)|0;

  RMSPreIndex = MEMORY.alloc_memory(rms_alloc);
  RMSPostIndex = MEMORY.alloc_memory(rms_alloc);

  RMSPre.RMS_init(RMSPreIndex, rms_max_count);
  RMSPost.RMS_init(RMSPostIndex, rms_max_count);

  RMSSCIndex = MEMORY.alloc_memory(rms_alloc);
  RMSSidechain.RMS_init(RMSSCIndex, rms_max_count);

  // FMA fma.11: legacy "Linear Phase" value (2) maps to HQ (1); ECO stays 0
  Quality >= 1.5 ? Quality = 1;
  set_oversample(Quality);

  // Visible frequency limit (FMA Edition B11: derived from the actual Nyquist)
  MAX_FREQ = srate / 2.0;
  MIN_FREQ = 10;
  FREQ_LOG_MAX = log(MAX_FREQ / MIN_FREQ);

  MAX_Q = 40;
  MIN_Q = 0.10;
  Q_LOG_MAX = log(MAX_Q / MIN_Q);

  DB_EQ_RANGE = 18;
  DB_EQ_RANGE_STEPS = 6;

  OLD_WIDTH = 0;

  button_focus = -1;

  gfx_mode = 1;
  gfx_clear = 0;

  read_freq = 0;

  click_up = 0;
  click_time = 0;

  selected_node = -1;
  selected_node_group = 0;

  node_drag_mode = 0;
  node_drag = 0;
  node_drag_offx = 0;
  node_drag_offy = 0;
  node_drag_stablex = 0;
  node_drag_stabley = 0;
  node_drag_mouse_speed = 6;
  node_drag_lock = 0;

  gainDb = 1;
  gainML = 1;
  gainSR = 1;

  initialise_gfx = 0;

  do_listen = 0;
  listen_width = 0.10;
  listen_q = 0.7071;
  listen_group = 0;
  listen_gain = db_to_gain(0);
  listen_filter.svf_set_sample_rate(srate);
  listen_filter.svf_bypass();
  listen_node = -1;

  listen_filter.a1 = listen_filter.t_a1;
  listen_filter.a2 = listen_filter.t_a2;
  listen_filter.a3 = listen_filter.t_a3;

  listen_filter.m0 = listen_filter.t_m0;
  listen_filter.m1 = listen_filter.t_m1;
  listen_filter.m2 = listen_filter.t_m2;
  listen_filter.iter_t = 1.0;

  // Define filter index numbers
  FILTER_PEAK = 0;
  FILTER_LOW_CUT = 1;
  FILTER_LOW_CUT_BUTTERWORTH = 2;
  FILTER_LOW_SHELF = 3;
  FILTER_HIGH_SHELF = 4;
  FILTER_HIGH_CUT = 5;
  FILTER_HIGH_CUT_BUTTERWORTH = 6;
  FILTER_NOTCH = 7;
  FILTER_BAND_PASS = 8;
  FILTER_TILT_SHELF = 9;
  FILTER_PULTEC_LOW_SHELF = 10;
  FILTER_ALL_PASS = 11;
  FILTER_LOW_CUT_ANALOG = 12;
  FILTER_HIGH_CUT_ANALOG = 13;

  // Define filter display order
  FilterTypes = MEMORY.alloc_memory(14);
  FilterTypes[0] = "Peak";
  FilterTypes[1] = "Low Cut";
  FilterTypes[2] = "Low Cut (Butterworth)";
  FilterTypes[3] = "Low Channel (Analog)";
  FilterTypes[4] = "Low Shelf";
  FilterTypes[5] = "High Shelf";
  FilterTypes[6] = "High Cut";
  FilterTypes[7] = "High Cut (Butterworth)";
  FilterTypes[8] = "High Channel (Analog)";
  FilterTypes[9] = "Notch";
  FilterTypes[10] = "Band Pass";
  FilterTypes[11] = "Tilt Shelf";
  FilterTypes[12] = "Pultec Low Shelf";
  FilterTypes[13] = "All Pass";

  // Define mapping from display order to index
  FilterMappingTo = MEMORY.alloc_memory(14);
  FilterMappingTo[0] = 0;
  FilterMappingTo[1] = 1;
  FilterMappingTo[2] = 2;
  FilterMappingTo[3] = 12;
  FilterMappingTo[4] = 3;
  FilterMappingTo[5] = 4;
  FilterMappingTo[6] = 5;
  FilterMappingTo[7] = 6;
  FilterMappingTo[8] = 13;
  FilterMappingTo[9] = 7;
  FilterMappingTo[10] = 8;
  FilterMappingTo[11] = 9;
  FilterMappingTo[12] = 10;
  FilterMappingTo[13] = 11;

  // Define mapping from index to display order
  FilterMappingFrom = MEMORY.alloc_memory(14);
  FilterMappingFrom[0] = 0;
  FilterMappingFrom[1] = 1;
  FilterMappingFrom[2] = 2;
  FilterMappingFrom[3] = 4;
  FilterMappingFrom[4] = 5;
  FilterMappingFrom[5] = 6;
  FilterMappingFrom[6] = 7;
  FilterMappingFrom[7] = 9;
  FilterMappingFrom[8] = 10;
  FilterMappingFrom[9] = 11;
  FilterMappingFrom[10] = 12;
  FilterMappingFrom[11] = 13;
  FilterMappingFrom[12] = 3;
  FilterMappingFrom[13] = 8;

  NumFilterSlopes = 10;
  FilterSlopes = MEMORY.alloc_memory(10);
  FilterSlopes[0] = "6dB";
  FilterSlopes[1] = "12dB";
  FilterSlopes[2] = "18dB";
  FilterSlopes[3] = "24dB";
  FilterSlopes[4] = "30dB";
  FilterSlopes[5] = "36dB";
  FilterSlopes[6] = "48dB";
  FilterSlopes[7] = "72dB";
  FilterSlopes[8] = "96dB";
  FilterSlopes[9] = "120dB";

  StereoModes = MEMORY.alloc_memory(3);
  StereoModes[0] = "Stereo";
  StereoModes[1] = "Mid";
  StereoModes[2] = "Side";
  StereoModes[3] = "Left";
  StereoModes[4] = "Right";

  // Automatic Gain Control
  agcControl = 0;
  agcOverride = 0;

  compact_width = 0;
  compact_height = 0;
  very_compact_width = 0;
  very_compact_height = 0;

  ShowPanel = PanelEnabled;
);

@slider

// FMA fma.11: legacy "Linear Phase" value (2) maps to HQ (1); ECO stays 0
Quality >= 1.5 ? Quality = 1;
set_oversample(Quality);

// FMA Edition B11: keep the frequency mapping in sync
// if the sample rate changes while the plugin is alive
MAX_FREQ = srate / 2.0;
FREQ_LOG_MAX = log(MAX_FREQ / MIN_FREQ);
spectrum.max_freq = srate / 2.0;
spectrum.freq_log_max = log(spectrum.max_freq / spectrum.min_freq);

button_oversample.select = Quality;
button_stereo_mode.select = Stereo_Mode;

gainDb = 2 ^ (Gain/6);
gainML = 2 ^ (MLGain/6);
gainSR = 2 ^ (SRGain/6);

// Mark filters for update if sliders have changed
Band_Enabled[0] != Node1_Enabled || Band_Type[0] != Node1_Type || Band_Gain[0] != Node1_Gain || Band_Frequency[0] != per_to_freq(Node1_Frequency,100) || Band_Q[0] != Node1_Q || Band_Slope[0] != Node1_Slope ? flag_filter_update(0);
Band_Enabled[1] != Node2_Enabled || Band_Type[1] != Node2_Type || Band_Gain[1] != Node2_Gain || Band_Frequency[1] != per_to_freq(Node2_Frequency,100) || Band_Q[1] != Node2_Q || Band_Slope[1] != Node2_Slope ? flag_filter_update(1);
Band_Enabled[2] != Node3_Enabled || Band_Type[2] != Node3_Type || Band_Gain[2] != Node3_Gain || Band_Frequency[2] != per_to_freq(Node3_Frequency,100) || Band_Q[2] != Node3_Q || Band_Slope[2] != Node3_Slope ? flag_filter_update(2);
Band_Enabled[3] != Node4_Enabled || Band_Type[3] != Node4_Type || Band_Gain[3] != Node4_Gain || Band_Frequency[3] != per_to_freq(Node4_Frequency,100) || Band_Q[3] != Node4_Q || Band_Slope[3] != Node4_Slope ? flag_filter_update(3);
Band_Enabled[4] != Node5_Enabled || Band_Type[4] != Node5_Type || Band_Gain[4] != Node5_Gain || Band_Frequency[4] != per_to_freq(Node5_Frequency,100) || Band_Q[4] != Node5_Q || Band_Slope[4] != Node5_Slope ? flag_filter_update(4);

// Update any automation
sliders_to_filters();



update_state();

@serialize

file_avail(handle) >= 0 ? (
  // Read mode
  file_var(0, version);

  version >= 100 ? ( // FMA Etapa 2: Thr gated on >= 110 below
    file_var(0, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Enabled, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Group, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Type, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Frequency, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Gain, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Q, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Slope, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Dynamic_Range, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Red, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Green, numBands);
    file_mem(0, Band_Blue, numBands);
    version >= 110 ? file_mem(0, Band_Dynamic_Thr, numBands); // FMA Etapa 2
    version >= 111 ? ( // FMA Etapa 2.1: per-band dynamics on/off + ATK/REL
      file_mem(0, Band_DynOn, numBands);
      file_mem(0, Band_Dyn_Atk, numBands);
      file_mem(0, Band_Dyn_Rel, numBands);
    );

  ) : (
    // Old version that has no version number
    // We've already read the first value and it wasn't a version
    // number, it's the enabled status for band 0
    Band_Enabled[0] = version;
    file_mem(0, Band_Enabled+1, 7);
    file_mem(0, Band_Group, 8);
    file_mem(0, Band_Type, 8);
    file_mem(0, Band_Frequency, 8);
    file_mem(0, Band_Gain, 8);
    file_mem(0, Band_Q, 8);
    file_mem(0, Band_Slope, 8);
    file_mem(0, Band_Dynamic_Range, 8);
    file_mem(0, Band_Red, 8);
    file_mem(0, Band_Green, 8);
    file_mem(0, Band_Blue, 8);
  );

  // FMA Etapa 2.1 migration: sessions saved by v1.2.0-fma.2 armed dynamics
  // with a non-zero range; carry that meaning into the new ON/OFF flag.
  // ATK/REL keep their in-memory defaults (10/100 ms) for old sessions.
  version >= 100 && version < 111 ? (
    fma_tmp_b = 0;
    while(fma_tmp_b < NUM_BANDS) (
      Band_Dynamic_Range[fma_tmp_b] != 0 ? Band_DynOn[fma_tmp_b] = 1;
      fma_tmp_b += 1;
    );
  );

) : (
  // Write mode
  // The version number should reflect the ReEQ version when the file
  // format changed.
  version = 111; // FMA Etapa 2.1: adds Band_DynOn + Band_Dyn_Atk/Rel

  file_var(0, version);
  file_var(0, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Enabled, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Group, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Type, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Frequency, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Gain, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Q, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Slope, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Dynamic_Range, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Red, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Green, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Blue, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Dynamic_Thr, NUM_BANDS); // FMA Etapa 2: requires version >= 110
  file_mem(0, Band_DynOn, NUM_BANDS); // FMA Etapa 2.1: requires version >= 111
  file_mem(0, Band_Dyn_Atk, NUM_BANDS);
  file_mem(0, Band_Dyn_Rel, NUM_BANDS);
);

flag_filter_update_all();

filters_to_sliders();

@block

// Get array accessed variables per block to make access faster
// in @sample section

update_audio_filters();

fma_block_maintain(); // FMA Etapa 2: dynamics bookkeeping

Band_Process0 = (Band_Enabled[0] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band1.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process1 = (Band_Enabled[1] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band2.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process2 = (Band_Enabled[2] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band3.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process3 = (Band_Enabled[3] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band4.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process4 = (Band_Enabled[4] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band5.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process5 = (Band_Enabled[5] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band6.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process6 = (Band_Enabled[6] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band7.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process7 = (Band_Enabled[7] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band8.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process8 = (Band_Enabled[8] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band9.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process9 = (Band_Enabled[9] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band10.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process10 = (Band_Enabled[10] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band11.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process11 = (Band_Enabled[11] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band12.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process12 = (Band_Enabled[12] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band13.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process13 = (Band_Enabled[13] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band14.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process14 = (Band_Enabled[14] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band15.filter.svf_is_resting();
Band_Process15 = (Band_Enabled[15] == BAND_STATE_ENABLED) || !band16.filter.svf_is_resting();

Band_Group0 = Band_Group[0];
Band_Group1 = Band_Group[1];
Band_Group2 = Band_Group[2];
Band_Group3 = Band_Group[3];
Band_Group4 = Band_Group[4];
Band_Group5 = Band_Group[5];
Band_Group6 = Band_Group[6];
Band_Group7 = Band_Group[7];
Band_Group8 = Band_Group[8];
Band_Group9 = Band_Group[9];
Band_Group10 = Band_Group[10];
Band_Group11 = Band_Group[11];
Band_Group12 = Band_Group[12];
Band_Group13 = Band_Group[13];
Band_Group14 = Band_Group[14];
Band_Group15 = Band_Group[15];

Listen_Process = do_listen || listen_node != -1 || !listen_filter.svf_is_resting();

agcControl = AGCEnabled;

@sample

// FMA Edition B11/B8: the true sample rate is only visible on the audio
// thread - @init/@slider/@block can observe the default rate (44100)
// instead of the real one (verified during offline renders). The first
// time the real rate is seen, re-derive everything that depends on it.
srate != fma_last_srate ? (
  fma_last_srate = srate;
  // FMA fma.11: legacy "Linear Phase" value (2) maps to HQ (1)
  Quality >= 1.5 ? Quality = 1;
  set_oversample(Quality);
  // B11: frequency mapping follows the actual Nyquist
  MAX_FREQ = srate / 2.0;
  FREQ_LOG_MAX = log(MAX_FREQ / MIN_FREQ);
  spectrum.max_freq = srate / 2.0;
  spectrum.freq_log_max = log(spectrum.max_freq / spectrum.min_freq);
  sliders_to_filters();
  flag_filter_update_all();
  update_audio_filters();
);

function encodeMS(l, r, mid*, side*) ( 
  mid = (l+r) * 0.5;
  side = (l-r) * 0.5;
);

function decodeMS(mid, side, l*, r*) (
  l = mid + side;
  r = mid - side;
);

spl0 += 0.0000000001; // DeNorm fix
spl1 += 0.0000000001; // DeNorm fix

spl0orig = spl0;
spl1orig = spl1;

// FMA Etapa 2: per-band dynamics detector (peak envelope on bandpass tap)
fma_dyn_armed ? (
  fma_det_in = (spl0orig + spl1orig) * 0.5 + 0.0000000001;
  Band_DynArmed[0] ? (
    fma_det_y = DetB0[0]*fma_det_in + DetB1[0]*DetX1[0] + DetB2[0]*DetX2[0] - DetA1[0]*DetY1[0] - DetA2[0]*DetY2[0];
    DetX2[0] = DetX1[0]; DetX1[0] = fma_det_in;
    DetY2[0] = DetY1[0]; DetY1[0] = fma_det_y;
    fma_det_a = abs(fma_det_y);
    fma_det_e = DetEnv[0];
    fma_det_e += (fma_det_a - fma_det_e) * (fma_det_a > fma_det_e ? DetAtk[0] : DetRel[0]);
    DetEnv[0] = fma_det_e;
  );
  Band_DynArmed[1] ? (
    fma_det_y = DetB0[1]*fma_det_in + DetB1[1]*DetX1[1] + DetB2[1]*DetX2[1] - DetA1[1]*DetY1[1] - DetA2[1]*DetY2[1];
    DetX2[1] = DetX1[1]; DetX1[1] = fma_det_in;
    DetY2[1] = DetY1[1]; DetY1[1] = fma_det_y;
    fma_det_a = abs(fma_det_y);
